 produced\n      comprehensive findings with code examples, references, and concrete recommendations - more\n      efficient than inline research\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-24T05:50:41.900Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFQ8W7Q3TWT541VNMTYNQ38M\n    type: success\n    content: \"Capturing scope expansion immediately: When debugging revealed architectural issues beyond\n      task scope, captured to inbox then promoted to proper task with full research context.\n      Prevented context loss.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-24T05:50:50.083Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFR0M0HQEPB9ZJ80HSF1H4R9\n    type: success\n    content: Iterative question-based design with AskUserQuestion tool - asking one design question at a\n      time during spec work (X-Kspec-Dir header choice, PID location, etc.) kept decisions focused\n      and got clear answers. Better than presenting all options at once.\n    created_at: 2026-01-24T12:45:46.424Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFR0MBH2Z9GKP96DPTW9J5HN\n    type: success\n    content: Subagent plan review before spec finalization - having a Plan subagent review the spec plan\n      caught gaps (missing error cases, race conditions, path validation) that would have been\n      harder to fix after writing the spec. Worth making standard practice for architecture specs.\n    created_at: 2026-01-24T12:45:57.667Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFR0MNJTDJ7SGWN2PWCPY5BA\n    type: friction\n    content: Didn't know about existing CLI features - wrote 36 ACs inline in YAML instead of using\n      'kspec item ac add', ran 29 individual 'task set --automation' instead of using --refs batch\n      mode. Need better CLI feature discovery or habit of checking --help first.\n    created_at: 2026-01-24T12:46:07.963Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Learning experience - established pattern of checking --help and using batch operations\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T05:18:26.718Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KFRAKC9HG1YD6192H0XJNFBW\n    type: success\n    content: \"Plan-Review-Revise cycle with subagents: Having a Plan agent design specs, then a second\n      Plan agent review for gaps with full user constraint context, then fixing issues before\n      presenting to user. Caught critical issues like ambiguous subagent spawn trigger.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-24T15:40:11.442Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFRAKVW1Q6E5FY9PTRFHXGA6\n    type: success\n    content: \"Incremental question-based requirements via AskUserQuestion: Asking one focused question\n      at a time (task selection order, subagent model, skill invocation, error tracking) kept\n      decisions clear and avoided ambiguity in spec design.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-24T15:40:27.393Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFRCQHCS2Z9Y0XCKFYKT1K8Z\n    type: success\n    content: \"Using testUlid() helper for test fixtures prevents silent failures from invalid Crockford\n      base32 chars (L, I, O, U). The helper auto-replaces these with valid chars. PR #210 adds\n      documentation for this pattern.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-24T16:17:24.889Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFS6AX4BHF071F63S4PTPGMS\n    type: success\n    content: E2E test creation workflow worked smoothly. Pattern established in project-selector.spec.ts\n      provided clear template for documentary tests. Using test.skip() for pending implementation is\n      effective for capturing expected behavior before UI exists. All 17 tests passed structure\n      validation on first run.\n    created_at: 2026-01-24T23:44:53.899Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFS6P9Q1GDVYAXF1E3ZGJTPZ\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Workflow runs accumulate without lifecycle management. 34+ active runs exist with no clear\n      way to complete/cancel old runs. Need: kspec workflow complete/cancel/cleanup commands to\n      manage run lifecycle and prevent stale run accumulation.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-24T23:51:07.233Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFST4YEZ7C3FYCFXAFTGKP09\n    type: success\n    content: \"Subagent audit pattern: Spawn agent to analyze multiple tasks → get structured findings →\n      act on findings. Effective for task/test audits where parallel exploration needed.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T05:31:10.176Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFST50NYXR9Q7TB9A3JC92F8\n    type: success\n    content: \"Task reframing pattern: Change 'Write tests for X' to 'Implement X (AC-N to AC-M)' with\n      implementation steps, required testIds, and 'No test.skip()' in Definition of Done. Prevents\n      documentary test anti-pattern.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T05:31:12.447Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFST52N598B4EQ4P2F2G2K2M\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Documentary test anti-pattern: Agents write test.skip() tests that pass CI but don't\n      verify anything. Task framing as 'write tests' enables this. Root cause: tests treated as goal\n      rather than validation mechanism.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T05:31:14.469Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFT1Q5Y5RNBFXXCB7DA8RGDF\n    type: success\n    content: \"Subagent delegation for git history recovery: Pattern of spawn agent → search git log -p\n      -S → extract lost content → report structured findings worked well for recovering 12+ lost\n      notes from merge. Effective when content exists in history but was overwritten.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T07:43:27.686Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFT1QE8X64CFNDSJ9ATEEB1Y\n    type: friction\n    content: Shadow branch divergence lacks guided resolution. When local and remote kspec-meta diverge\n      significantly (61 vs 362 commits), kspec shadow sync just fails with no guidance. Manual git\n      merge-tree diagnosis and conflict-by-conflict resolution required. @yaml-merge-driver would\n      help but was cancelled.\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T07:43:36.221Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTESK40ED91F97SCD76JP6W\n    type: success\n    content: \"Test-first development pattern: Writing comprehensive tests before integration\n      implementation catches edge cases early and provides clear specification. Pattern used in\n      loop-mode-error-handling task: (1) Created test file with 23 tests covering all 9 ACs, (2)\n      Implemented utilities to make tests pass, (3) Integrated into ralph.ts. Benefits: TypeScript\n      compilation errors caught immediately, edge cases identified before integration, tests serve\n      as executable documentation. This approach is especially valuable for complex logic with\n      multiple edge cases (failure tracking, progress detection, escalation thresholds).\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T11:31:58.208Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTFWFZ6370BPQ1GMZRVMTN3\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Automation-eligible tasks lack time/scope estimates. All eligible tasks in iteration 4\n      were large-scope (10+ ACs, 30-60+ min work). Automation loops work best with 10-15 min tasks\n      but selection mechanism doesn't filter by estimated effort. Existing eligibility system\n      addresses complexity/clarity but not time dimension. Result: loops start work that can't\n      complete in single iteration. Suggest: add estimated_effort field (small/medium/large) to\n      tasks, --max-effort flag for automation.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T11:51:01.863Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTFWS69M8GSAXS7TJZBKMEA\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Task Definition of Done (DoD) not visible during task selection. Task @01KFP84N had DoD\n      requirement 'All E2E tests pass - no skips' in notes but wasn't surfaced during ready task\n      selection. Workflow enforced DoD strictly at completion but constraint wasn't visible upfront.\n      Created situation where task appeared eligible but became non-completable mid-work. DoD\n      criteria are critical constraints that should influence task selection, not just exit\n      validation. Suggest: extract DoD to structured field, show in task list, filter tasks by DoD\n      compatibility.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T11:51:11.305Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTFX1MSXCMTBTYC05WD8NSY\n    type: success\n    content: \"Partial progress commits valuable in automation loops. Iteration 4 on @01KFP84N: added\n      test IDs to components (fd70b86d) even though DoD required fully enabled tests. Committing\n      partial work provided value: (1) next iteration can continue from checkpoint, (2) incremental\n      progress visible in git history, (3) work not lost if task abandoned. Better than\n      all-or-nothing approach. Pattern: commit meaningful increments even if task incomplete,\n      document remaining work clearly in notes and commit message.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T11:51:19.962Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTFX9SDQQ7ZP5BC7E8SB821\n    type: success\n    content: \"Comprehensive session-end notes enable clean task handoffs. Final note on @01KFP84N\n      documented: what's done, what remains, estimated effort, specific next steps, blockers,\n      recommendations. This level of detail makes continuing work in next iteration frictionless -\n      no context rebuilding needed. Pattern: when leaving task in_progress, include (1) completed\n      work summary, (2) remaining work list, (3) effort estimate, (4) next concrete steps, (5)\n      blockers/considerations. Especially valuable in automation loops where next iteration may be\n      hours/days later.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T11:51:28.301Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTGC48BJC0A13Q7NW8SVJKX\n    type: friction\n    content: \"E2E test verification blocked by daemon requirement in automation loops. Pattern\n      encountered in @01KFP84N and @01KFP84S: (1) Adding data-testid attributes to components is\n      automatable, (2) Removing test.skip() is automatable, (3) Verifying tests actually pass\n      requires daemon running + test execution + debugging failures which exceeds single loop\n      iteration scope (est 30-60+ min). This creates a 3-phase workflow where phase 3 blocks\n      automation. Tasks remain in_progress at ~70% completion awaiting human verification.\n      Solutions: daemon auto-start infrastructure, task splitting (separate test ID addition from\n      verification), or DoD adjustment for automation eligibility.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T11:59:34.155Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Addressed by task @01KG5VSF\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-29T21:51:19.232Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KFTGKVRXEEV5MBV1XH1XQ39T\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Loop iteration 6 encountered systematic blockers: All eligible P2 tasks are web UI E2E\n      tests requiring daemon startup + test verification, exceeding single iteration capacity. Both\n      in-progress tasks (@01KFP84N, @01KFP84S) hit same blocker (daemon requirement) and now at\n      failure count 2. Attempted @01KFMMXF (export command) but ~300-500 line implementation scope\n      also exceeds capacity. Pattern suggests: (1) Web UI E2E tasks incorrectly marked\n      automation:eligible - should be automation:needs_review until daemon automation exists, OR (2)\n      Tasks should be split: 'Add test IDs' (automatable) + 'Verify E2E tests pass' (manual), OR (3)\n      DoD should be relaxed to 'Tests enabled, pending verification'.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T12:03:47.613Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTGRPJXF2K3EW6RRR2WY3WD\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Loop mode failure tracking not queryable: [LOOP-FAIL:N] notes exist but no CLI command to\n      check task failure count. Had to manually grep task notes to determine if @01KFP84N and\n      @01KFP84S hit 3-failure threshold (both at count 2). Needed for automation decision: should\n      loop retry task or escalate to automation:needs_review? Suggest: kspec task get @ref\n      --loop-failures or similar to return failure count.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T12:06:26.141Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTH5GC9955K0HDD6V0MXSGT\n    type: success\n    content: \"Loop error handling protocol (PR #243) executed correctly in iteration 7: [LOOP-FAIL:N]\n      notes tracked failures per task, failure count visible across iterations, auto-escalation to\n      automation:needs_review triggered at threshold 3. Pattern enables clear visibility into which\n      tasks are struggling in automation and systematic escalation when human intervention needed.\n      Tasks @01KFP84N and @01KFP84S hit 3rd failure (daemon requirement blocker) and were properly\n      escalated.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T12:13:25.769Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTHK60JWKZKH928E6QVZ6TF\n    type: friction\n    content: \"E2E test tasks hit systematic blocker in automation loops: Cannot run daemon (npm run\n      serve) + E2E tests (npm run test:e2e) within loop constraints. Pattern affects all web UI E2E\n      test tasks. Results in [LOOP-FAIL] notes and automation:needs_review escalation. Encountered\n      on tasks 01KFP84N, 01KFP84S, 01KFP84X in iteration 8. Implementation completes successfully\n      (test IDs + test files), but verification step requires human-driven session with long-running\n      daemon.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T12:20:53.906Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTHKCY5R1K8N136P1HH3Y3J\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Session checkpoint hook blocks exit when in_progress tasks have automation:needs_review\n      status. Hook expects all in_progress tasks to either complete or have handoff notes. However,\n      tasks marked automation:needs_review are intentionally paused for human review. Workaround:\n      manually add comprehensive handoff notes before exit. Pattern suggests automation:needs_review\n      should either auto-add handoff notes or be recognized as valid exit state.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T12:21:00.997Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTHKM3WR00TD31129KQEMAF\n    type: success\n    content: Task-work-loop workflow provided effective structure for automation. Clear steps (filter\n      eligible → select → verify → start → work → commit → submit → PR → exit) prevented skipped\n      steps. Workflow state tracking enabled clean handoffs. Successfully completed inbox view\n      implementation (01KFP84X) following all steps systematically.\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T12:21:08.348Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTJNAK1HV8NJKQCSB767QS5\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Automation loop cannot verify E2E tests that require daemon running. Pattern: Tasks add\n      data-testid attributes and create E2E tests, but verification requires manual session to start\n      daemon (npm run serve -w packages/web-ui) and run tests. Repeated across @01KFP84N (tasks\n      view), @01KFP84S (items view), @01KFP84X (inbox view) in session 01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3.\n      Tasks marked automation:needs_review and stall at ~70-80% complete. Potential solutions:\n      headless daemon fixture for E2E tests, mock API layer, or split tasks (implementation +\n      verification).\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T12:39:32.705Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTJNJYX2PHTGXCAG3KA0M7Y\n    type: success\n    content: \"Task-work workflow (@task-work-loop) successfully enforced complete task lifecycle in\n      automation loop: task selection from eligible list, verification before start, implementation\n      with notes during work, DoD validation, commit with trailers, submit to pending_review, PR\n      creation. Session 01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3 iteration 9 completed @01KFP850 (command palette\n      E2E tests) from start to PR without friction. Workflow prevented common mistakes: starting\n      without verification, skipping notes, missing DoD checks.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T12:39:41.277Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTKCK1P5GTM073CM64X5WTM\n    type: success\n    content: \"Task verification pattern: Before starting test-only task (01KFP854 - E2E tests), verified\n      WebSocketManager implementation existed. Read manager.ts to confirm AC coverage (ac-28 to\n      ac-32) before committing to E2E test creation. This prevented wasting iteration on tests for\n      non-existent features. Pattern: For tasks scoped as 'write tests for X', verify X\n      implementation exists first. Especially valuable in automation loops with limited iteration\n      budget.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T12:52:15.031Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTMKWW95BXAHA9TF79XT9MR\n    type: success\n    content: \"Batching related E2E test tasks into a single PR branch: Completed 3 tasks (@01KFP85D\n      observations panel, @01KFP85G error handling, @01KFP85M navigation) on feature branch\n      feat/observations-panel-e2e-tests. All tasks involved E2E tests and data-testid attributes for\n      web UI. Benefits: (1) Avoided multiple PR context switches and branch overhead, (2) Shared\n      commits across tasks (e.g., error-message testid used by all 3), (3) Coherent scope for\n      review. Pattern works when tasks are tightly related, share common files, and can be reviewed\n      together. Session completed 4 tasks total efficiently using this approach.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T13:13:43.049Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTP0GJKNPDMH60GSPXD95P0\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Automation loop cannot handle daemon-dependent E2E test verification. Pattern: Tasks get\n      to ~80-85% complete (implementation done, test IDs added, tests enabled) but then block on\n      daemon startup + iterative test debugging. Three tasks hit this in session\n      01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3 (iteration 14): @01KFP84N, @01KFP84S, @01KFQAGY. Root cause: Daemon\n      requires manual 'npm run serve', E2E failures unpredictable, debugging cycle exceeds\n      single-iteration capacity. Workaround: Mark automation:needs_review and exit loop. Impact: Web\n      UI E2E testing tasks systematically blocked from automation completion. Potential solutions:\n      (1) Automate daemon lifecycle in loop, (2) Split tasks into 'implementation' + 'E2E\n      verification' phases, (3) Add automation:daemon-required tag for better categorization.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T13:38:05.012Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTPN91A5V1A3NBC088WA5QE\n    type: friction\n    content: Task-work-loop workflow lacks exit condition for 'eligible but unsuitable' scenario. When\n      eligible tasks exist but all exceed single-iteration capacity (e.g., 5 P3 tasks requiring\n      300-500 lines each), workflow continues to step 4 (start task) with no clean exit path. Had to\n      manually cancel workflow in iteration 16. Exit conditions defined (no eligible tasks, already\n      done, work complete) but not 'all eligible tasks too complex'. Affects ralph when only complex\n      work remains in eligible pool.\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T13:49:25.418Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTPNH9WXC0G77CB9JDSM5C8\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Task automation eligibility assessment happens too late in workflow. Tasks get marked\n      automation:eligible without scope assessment. Automation loops then waste iterations doing\n      [LOOP-FAIL:1], [LOOP-FAIL:2], [LOOP-FAIL:3] assessments before marking\n      automation:needs_review. Example: task @01KFMMXF assessed in iterations 6, 7, 14 as too\n      complex (~300-500 lines) but stayed in eligible pool causing repeated evaluation. Assessment\n      should occur BEFORE tasks marked eligible, not after automation attempts them. Related to\n      @task-automation-eligibility but focuses on pre-eligibility workflow gap.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T13:49:33.884Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTPYK46Y190SQJC6RTA7HAA\n    type: success\n    content: \"Automation loop graceful exit: When tasks require daemon/multi-file coordination exceeding\n      loop capacity, system correctly escalated 3 tasks to automation:needs_review with\n      comprehensive handoff notes. Clean exit without attempting incomplete implementations. Session\n      01KFTDBQB3Z0PA5Y0GQD8T1RW3 iteration 17.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T13:54:30.663Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTPYVEK0ZQTH006HH1H5F1M\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Zero-completion automation sessions: Loop iteration 17 completed with 0 tasks finished,\n      all 3 in_progress tasks escalated to automation:needs_review. Distinct from prior successful\n      Ralph loops. Root cause: Tasks marked automation:eligible but require daemon E2E testing (2\n      tasks) or multi-file coordinated implementation (1 task). Gap between 'eligible' tag and\n      actual automation feasibility in single iteration. Affects task selection heuristics.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T13:54:39.187Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTQJ62852K34N95AFCKX5SC\n    type: success\n    content: \"Loop iteration 19 assessment: Correctly identified that all 4 eligible GitHub Pages export\n      tasks (@01KFMMJ4, @01KFMMXK, @01KFMMXR, @01KFMMXW) exceed automation loop capacity. Marked all\n      as automation:needs_review with clear reasoning. Tasks form a coordinated feature set\n      requiring multi-hour focused implementation.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T14:05:12.649Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTR8FDCNMBT7P0VNN8SDBSW\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Repetitive checkpoint notes across automation loops: Tasks stuck in\n      automation:needs_review state get identical checkpoint notes added every iteration. Example:\n      @01KFP84N received 36 notes, with notes 27-36 being nearly identical 'Loop Iteration N -\n      Session End Checkpoint' messages. Creates noise without adding value. Possible solutions: (1)\n      Skip checkpoint notes if last note is recent and task state unchanged, (2) Update most recent\n      checkpoint note instead of appending, (3) Add checkpoint command that manages session-end\n      state separately from progress notes.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T14:17:23.116Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTR8ZK3WJV841Y8F7C3KN9P\n    type: success\n    content: \"Loop iteration 21 efficiently completed pending_review task @01KFP85M in first action by\n      checking task status, validating work was already merged, and immediately completing it.\n      Demonstrates value of prioritizing pending_review tasks over in_progress tasks - they're\n      usually closest to done and just need verification/completion. Pattern: pending_review >\n      in_progress > ready.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T14:17:39.684Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTRRAAF4852S6F5H249P78G\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Automation loop iterations consumed even when zero eligible tasks exist. Pattern observed\n      in iteration 23: loop checked 3 in_progress tasks (all automation:needs_review), found 0\n      eligible ready tasks, added checkpoint notes, then exited. No actual work possible but\n      iteration budget still used for status quo documentation. Systemic issue - will recur whenever\n      queue is fully blocked on manual work. Potential improvement: early exit detection before\n      iteration starts, or iteration budget exemption for no-op sessions.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T14:26:02.191Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: \"Resolved by @01KFV6CZ (PR #247). Ralph loop now filters both ready AND in_progress\n      tasks by automation:eligible. Session 28 demonstrates clean exit when no eligible tasks remain\n      - zero redundant iterations.\"\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-26T01:13:03.331Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KFTRY6ASB4AHM7D0ZTP2HX68\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Loop mode runs redundant iterations when no progress possible. Iterations 22-24 added\n      identical checkpoint notes with no state changes. All 3 in_progress tasks marked\n      automation:needs_review, no eligible tasks available, but loop continued for 3 iterations\n      adding duplicate 'no progress possible' notes. Suggest: early exit condition 'if no state\n      change in last N iterations AND no eligible tasks, exit immediately' to avoid redundant work.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T14:29:14.713Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: \"Resolved by @01KFV6CZ (PR #247). Exit condition now checks automation eligibility for\n      both ready and in_progress tasks. Session 28 exited immediately when finding no eligible\n      work.\"\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-26T01:13:09.905Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KFTSQQSAEJ0HXNEQJ209YCRZ\n    type: friction\n    content: Workflow system lacks early exit mechanism. When workflow determines no work is possible\n      (e.g., no eligible tasks), must still step through all remaining workflow steps providing skip\n      reasons. Attempted 'kspec workflow complete @ref' which does not exist. Would benefit from\n      'workflow exit' or 'workflow skip-remaining' command to cleanly terminate when continuation is\n      impossible.\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T14:43:11.786Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTSR2MBYJQ6GAS3Y8Z4DBV4\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Automation loop adds repetitive status notes to stalled tasks. After 27 iterations of\n      ralph automation, same 3 in-progress tasks (@01KFP84N, @01KFP84S, @01KFQAGY) accumulated 27+\n      nearly-identical notes documenting 'Loop Iteration N - No Eligible Tasks'. While notes provide\n      audit trail, they create significant noise obscuring substantive progress notes. Consider:\n      batch note update mechanism, dedicated status/stall-reason field, or suppress iteration notes\n      when status unchanged.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T14:43:22.891Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTSWYG75X3E38BWWRK8HBWQ\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Ralph loop ran 28 iterations with identical outcome (no eligible tasks, same 3 tasks\n      documented each time). After 2-3 consecutive iterations returning no eligible tasks, the loop\n      should recognize the pattern and exit early. Current behavior wastes API calls and adds\n      redundant notes. Need early termination logic: if last N iterations (N=2 or 3) all exited with\n      'no eligible tasks' and same task set, stop the loop.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T14:46:02.504Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFTTA3TFQ6MBC3CZ2Z1V740J\n    type: success\n    content: \"Structured loop iteration note template pattern: Used consistently across 30 automation\n      iterations to document why progress wasn't possible. Template format: '## Loop Iteration N -\n      [Status]' followed by Exit Reason, Task Status (with ✅/❌ checkboxes for completed/incomplete\n      work), specific blockers, and clear next actions. Creates audit trail showing automation\n      decision-making and prevents false 'why is nothing happening' concerns. Makes it obvious when\n      automation is correctly identifying blockers vs stuck in broken logic.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T14:53:13.935Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVPXSZXJE3FNK50A1M0MYN8\n    type: friction\n    content: E2E tests in packages/web-ui timeout after 2+ minutes with no progress indication or\n      diagnostic output. Makes debugging test failures extremely difficult - cannot iterate rapidly.\n      Tests may be waiting on daemon startup that never completes, or Playwright fixtures have\n      configuration issues. Blocked work on @01KFP84N and @01KFP84S in loop iteration 2.\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T23:13:19.358Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Addressed by task @01KG5VSF\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-29T21:51:17.744Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KFVPY36ARRRWYKQZTRXC8CAX\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Loop mode task verification gap: Multiple iterations accepted task notes claiming 'already\n      implemented' or 'tests exist' without independent verification (running tests, checking code).\n      Iteration 1 concluded UI was incomplete based on test failures; iteration 2 found UI\n      components actually exist with proper test IDs. Real issue was E2E infrastructure, not missing\n      implementation. Task notes are context, not proof of completion.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T23:13:28.778Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVPYB4RSBEGW5GF5Z7W1WY8\n    type: success\n    content: \"Reading actual source code to verify task claims proved more reliable than trusting notes.\n      When @01KFP84N notes said 'UI incomplete', reading TaskList.svelte revealed all required test\n      IDs were present. Verification approach: Read components -> check test IDs -> run tests (if\n      possible) -> only then accept completion claims. This prevented false conclusions about\n      missing implementation.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T23:13:36.921Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVQKD22NWCRJFJWRBKPNDR0\n    type: success\n    content: \"E2E tests via Playwright for daemon API endpoints: Using\n      packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/*.spec.ts for real HTTP integration tests (not vitest mocks) aligns\n      with project architecture documented in AGENTS.md. This session: created api-projects.spec.ts\n      with 5 passing tests making real fetch() calls to running daemon. Pattern: Start daemon via\n      test fixture, make HTTP requests, verify responses. More reliable than mocking and tests\n      actual behavior.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T23:25:07.010Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVQKFHX5SX08ZQZDX25MKJS\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Task DoD conflict with project conventions: Task @01KFQAF9 DoD said 'write real HTTP\n      tests' and 'no documentary/stub tests remain' but AGENTS.md documents that daemon API routes\n      use documentary tests (static analysis). Had to resolve conflict by checking existing patterns\n      in daemon-api-*.test.ts files. Resolution: Created E2E tests in packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/ and\n      updated documentary test to reference them. Friction point: When DoD contradicts documented\n      patterns, unclear which is authoritative.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T23:25:09.566Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVQYR778DPEYXP93M0JKW0V\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Loop mode error handling AC-5 not working: Tasks @01KFP84N, @01KFP84S, @01KFQAGY all have\n      [LOOP-FAIL:3] notes but remain automation:eligible instead of being auto-escalated to\n      automation:needs_review as specified in @loop-mode-error-handling AC-5. Implementation in PR\n      #243 claims to handle this but actual behavior shows automation status not being updated after\n      3 failures. Verified in session 01KFVN3DDTKEQF1DAF8V3KV48V iteration 4.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T23:31:18.887Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVRK63DF261C4ZNK9NWQJJX\n    type: success\n    content: \"Loop iteration 5: Accountability in action - instead of immediately marking tasks as\n      needs_review, actually debugged E2E infrastructure issues. Fixed real problems (Vite proxy\n      configuration, API client URL handling) that were blocking all E2E tests. Committed working\n      code (c24fd694) that moves the project forward. Loop failures should document genuine\n      investigation and progress, not just 'this is hard, skipping.'\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T23:42:28.461Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVSBZ9AKZY33E0SAYB9KJEK\n    type: success\n    content: \"E2E test infrastructure debugging pattern: When E2E tests fail, work backward through the\n      stack systematically. Session 01KFVN3D example: test timeout → Vite proxy missing → API client\n      hardcoded URLs → daemon fixture loading issue. At each layer, verify the fix (tests connect\n      successfully) before moving to next layer. This methodical approach identified root cause\n      (daemon ContextManager path handling) after fixing intermediate issues (Vite proxy + relative\n      URLs in commit c24fd694).\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-25T23:56:00.682Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVSKKCZVQ2K2BRJMT0A86WP\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Loop mode automation tag disconnect: Across 8 consecutive loop iterations, task notes\n      documented 'marked automation:needs_review' but the actual command 'kspec task set @ref\n      --automation needs_review' was never executed. This suggests a pattern in autonomous loops\n      where intent is documented in notes but the corresponding state change command is not run.\n      Root cause: loop documenting WHAT should happen without executing HOW to make it happen.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T00:00:10.655Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVTBAYZ7S0403M97E2XG31T\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Ralph loop iteration without progress: Loop ran 12 consecutive iterations with zero code\n      changes or git commits. All iterations exited with 'no automation-eligible tasks' message.\n      Tasks remained in_progress state throughout despite being marked automation:needs_review. Each\n      iteration added near-identical checkpoint notes documenting 'no work attempted'. Pattern\n      indicates need for circuit breaker that detects repeated no-progress iterations and either\n      auto-escalates tasks or stops the loop. Related to @01KF554T circuit breaker concept but\n      captures actual observed behavior rather than theoretical design.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T00:13:08.448Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVTBKBKDNJ0HJ6VMJ9AXQMH\n    type: success\n    content: \"Session checkpoint hook enforcement prevented task abandonment: Stop hook detected 3\n      in_progress tasks without recent meaningful progress and blocked session exit until checkpoint\n      notes were added. All tasks received documentation of current state, blockers, and next steps.\n      This pattern ensures tasks don't silently stall - they either get documented or completed.\n      Hook runs automatically on session end with no manual intervention needed. Particularly\n      valuable for automation loops where task state must be explicit for next iteration.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T00:13:17.043Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVTYSJECRND016ZATZ25N3A\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Ralph loop continues iterating when all active tasks are automation:needs_review. Observed\n      across 15 consecutive iterations: each iteration runs 'kspec tasks ready --eligible', finds 0\n      tasks, then adds repetitive status notes to all escalated tasks. Exit condition correctly\n      identifies no eligible work but doesn't trigger early exit before status documentation.\n      Result: unnecessary API calls, note bloat (45+ notes across 3 tasks), slower session\n      completion. Ideal: exit immediately when no eligible tasks remain without adding iteration\n      notes to needs_review tasks.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T00:23:45.998Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: \"Resolved by @01KFV6CZ (PR #247). Ralph loop now correctly exits when all in_progress\n      tasks are automation:needs_review. Verified in session 28.\"\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-26T01:13:16.392Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KFVTYW9TT5NNV7JNR0PHRM0R\n    type: success\n    content: \"Task escalation with comprehensive rationale prevents false automation work. Pattern\n      observed: when tasks blocked or require human decisions, automation loop adds multi-paragraph\n      notes documenting: (1) WHAT blocks the work, (2) WHY it's not automatable, (3) WHAT human\n      needs to do next. Tags task automation:needs_review. Result: zero false work attempts across\n      15 iterations, clear handoff context for human sessions. Quality over speed: better to\n      escalate with context than attempt inappropriate work.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T00:23:48.795Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVVATF0YA11E7EB88TAHP3X\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Ralph automation loop ran 10+ iterations (7-17) with zero implementation work after all\n      tasks marked needs_review. Loop exit logic only checks task existence, not progress\n      stagnation. Should detect: N consecutive iterations with no file changes, commits, or task\n      status transitions → early exit with diagnostic.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T00:30:20.128Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVVB2KHS3P06SR1X42DFW7Q\n    type: success\n    content: \"Session checkpoint notes (iterations 7-17) consistently documented: task state, what's\n      complete, what's blocked, required resolution steps, investigation files, automation status.\n      This pattern provides excellent continuity for next session and clear audit trail of\n      escalation reasoning.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T00:30:28.466Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVVBBE6ED70C0ZKXW32Q97Z\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Daemon fixture loading blocker affected 2/3 tasks across 10 iterations with no alternative\n      approach attempted. Pattern: E2E test harness starts daemon with --kspec-dir pointing to temp\n      fixtures, daemon returns empty data instead of YAML content. Should have tried: run daemon\n      manually with debug output, inspect ContextManager code paths, create minimal reproduction\n      case, or escalate infrastructure debugging to separate focused task.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T00:30:37.511Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Promoted to task @01KG5VSF\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-29T21:51:11.063Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n    promoted_to: \"@01KG5VSF\"\n  - _ulid: 01KFVVHGHH2Q71ECC19CF59E4E\n    type: success\n    content: \"Loop mode escalation discipline working as designed: Session 01KFVN3D ran 18 iterations\n      with 3 in_progress tasks. All tasks marked automation:needs_review in iterations 7-8 after\n      assessment. Loop correctly exited when kspec tasks ready --eligible returned empty array. No\n      thrashing, no shortcuts attempted, no improper completion claims. Tasks stayed in_progress\n      with comprehensive checkpoint notes providing human handoff context. This validates the\n      automation system recognizing its limits and delegating complex/blocked work appropriately.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T00:33:59.346Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFVXSQF1YH0J7X5HPQHJDR8D\n    type: success\n    content: \"Ralph loop exit condition working correctly: Session 28 demonstrated clean exit behavior\n      after @01KFV6CZ fix. Loop checked 'kspec tasks ready --eligible', found empty array (all 3\n      in_progress tasks were automation:needs_review), and exited immediately with zero redundant\n      iterations. This resolves the overnight session issue where loops ran 30+ iterations with no\n      progress. Exit condition now filters both ready AND in_progress tasks by automation:eligible\n      status.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T01:13:25.730Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFXTADHRF0ZBX4E0HR7H11AS\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Tasks created via 'kspec derive' have auto-generated notes that just copy spec content.\n      For standalone tasks, needed to manually add structured sections: Background (why this\n      matters), Reproduction steps, Concrete examples, Open design questions. This structure makes\n      tasks actionable without conversation context.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T18:51:07.192Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFXTAKKXZ27TMK4SA7TQMAFG\n    type: success\n    content: Subagent plan review caught CLI command syntax issues (missing --as and --id flags) before\n      execution. Using a reviewer subagent after writing a plan prevents wasted iterations.\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T18:51:13.405Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFXVK5QBFCN3A3BTXME0G86C\n    type: friction\n    content: dist/daemon/ can become stale without warning - packages/daemon/src changes aren't\n      reflected until root 'npm run build' is run. E2E tests can pass web-ui build but fail because\n      daemon code is outdated. Wasted debugging time on what appeared to be runtime error but was\n      actually stale build.\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T19:13:22.667Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: \"Fixed in PR #276 - added daemon staleness detection that warns when dist/daemon is\n      older than source\"\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T02:03:06.384Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KFXVKJJE3JWG67VFYNM64ZC8\n    type: success\n    content: Comparing dist/ vs source when debugging daemon issues - immediately revealed the stale\n      build problem when runtime debugging was going in circles\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T19:13:35.823Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFYAH1CQ6FP9V5MJ4MMB33AW\n    type: success\n    content: \"Debug element technique for Svelte reactivity: Adding conditional debug elements like\n      `{#if state}<div data-testid=\\\"debug-...\\\">{state}</div>{/if}` quickly verifies whether state\n      is actually true at runtime vs expected. Useful for diagnosing reactivity issues where console\n      logs show updates but UI doesn't reflect them.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T23:34:21.335Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFYAH9ABXKZNRAWVN8G751YF\n    type: friction\n    content: \"bits-ui Sheet/Dialog Portal reactivity broken in Svelte 5: Props passed to child\n      components through bits-ui Portal don't update reactively. PresenceManager.shouldRender\n      returns false even when open=true. Workaround: use native elements or custom components\n      instead of bits-ui Dialog for Svelte 5 projects. See task @01KFP84N notes for full\n      investigation.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-26T23:34:29.452Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Resolved by using $state object pattern + flushSync. See @01KFZ708 and /svelte-5 skill\n      for documentation.\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-27T07:52:07.714Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KFZ3YG03R29D6MYRHFT5WV5S\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Task notes from loop mode sessions can become noisy/unreliable, requiring manual cleanup\n      or user warning to ignore recent notes. Example: @01KFP84N had 26 noise notes removed and user\n      warned remaining notes might be incorrect.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-27T06:58:36.675Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFZ3YNHQWZFZ6MMWBR81H6Y6\n    type: success\n    content: Using Explore subagent for deep analysis before making changes provided comprehensive\n      understanding (file locations, line numbers, root cause, impact analysis) that enabled\n      confident parallel fixes via multiple subagents.\n    created_at: 2026-01-27T06:58:42.360Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KFZ708S00S4EA95C1A57HHD2\n    type: success\n    content: \"Svelte 5 reactivity solution: Use $state object pattern + flushSync() for reactive\n      conditional rendering. Separate $state variables may not trigger {#if} block re-renders;\n      wrapping state in object (panel = $state({ open: false, task: null })) and using flushSync(()\n      => { panel.open = true }) ensures synchronous DOM updates. Also documented in /svelte-5 skill.\n      Resolves friction @01KFYAH9.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-27T07:52:00.544Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG031N6WQM6BM3S0J2YFEF0H\n    type: friction\n    content: \"bits-ui Select onValueChange in Svelte 5 returns array of characters plus new value (e.g.,\n      ['a','l','l','in_progress'] instead of 'in_progress'). Workaround: extract last element from\n      array when Array.isArray(value).\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-27T16:02:06.172Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Incorrect diagnosis - bits-ui Select works correctly; issue was likely misuse of spread\n      operator or other code error\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T05:14:58.910Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG031Y246EC054DSQ2CEX9SF\n    type: success\n    content: Console log capture in E2E tests revealed exact bits-ui callback values, making the array\n      quirk immediately visible. Adding console.log to component handlers during debugging is highly\n      effective for understanding Svelte 5 reactivity issues.\n    created_at: 2026-01-27T16:02:15.236Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG0J4H7FFW05RZP39YDBM2YF\n    type: success\n    content: Reading reference tests (tasks.spec.ts) before writing new tests - understanding existing\n      patterns informed structure and avoided reinventing conventions\n    created_at: 2026-01-27T20:25:49.040Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG0J4XRDKQ7Z6Y7FBP2TX1K8\n    type: success\n    content: Documenting blocking issues with specific symptoms, likely causes ranked by probability,\n      and debug commands - makes next session pickup much faster\n    created_at: 2026-01-27T20:26:01.869Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG0N4V90NDXX0MVSYXWWTN2M\n    type: friction\n    content: Schema validation (safeParse) failures in extractItemsFromRaw are silent - items just don't\n      appear in results with no error or warning. This caused significant debugging time when trait\n      had invalid enum values and module had nested items in traits field. Consider adding\n      validation error logging or a strict mode that throws on parse failures.\n    created_at: 2026-01-27T21:18:25.056Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG0ZHY1QR402HYBSWCMZJ9Z5\n    type: success\n    content: Dedicated E2E fixtures pattern - creating packages/web-ui/tests/fixtures/ separate from\n      shared tests/fixtures/ cleanly isolates E2E test data from unit tests, preventing\n      cross-contamination\n    created_at: 2026-01-28T00:20:19.639Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG17R6Y5MEF5DPZ1Z73YFJEW\n    type: success\n    content: Using /e2e skill patterns immediately caught ULID validation issue (Crockford base32\n      excludes I, L, O, U). Invalid ULIDs in fixtures fail silently - the skill's warning helped\n      debug quickly.\n    created_at: 2026-01-28T02:43:33.957Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG17RDSGDZB9X9XTRXN4458K\n    type: friction\n    content: Session context is loaded from .kspec-session file (not kynetic.meta.yaml). This caused\n      debugging time when E2E tests couldn't find session focus. The API (fetchSessionContext) and\n      file location should be documented in /e2e skill or AGENTS.md.\n    created_at: 2026-01-28T02:43:40.977Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG17RKW385KB2RXRV8KCAVWV\n    type: friction\n    content: TaskSummary interface was missing depends_on field, needed for dashboard to compute blocked\n      task count. Had to add to shared types + daemon routes. API contracts should include all\n      fields needed for common UI computations.\n    created_at: 2026-01-28T02:43:47.203Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Fixed - depends_on field added to TaskSummary interface and daemon routes\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T05:13:39.126Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG1GNQJZRR2F3TH526VHVA3A\n    type: friction\n    content: \"E2E skill has incorrect selector guidance for bits-ui Select: recommends\n      getByRole('option') but bits-ui uses data-slot attributes. Correct pattern: await\n      dropdownContent.locator('[data-slot=\\\"select-content\\\"]'); then\n      dropdownContent.locator('[data-slot=\\\"select-item\\\"]').filter({ hasText: 'value' }).click().\n      Update e2e/SKILL.md line 15 and lines 162-164.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-28T05:19:29.888Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: \"Fixed in PR #256 - updated E2E skill with correct bits-ui Select selector pattern\"\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-28T05:24:34.861Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG2FM29NVPRY5BF8DW52FQ00\n    type: success\n    content: isStaticMode() guard pattern worked well for conditionally disabling features without major\n      refactoring - single check at API layer propagates through entire app\n    created_at: 2026-01-28T14:20:21.173Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG4M2HRF76XZRXKVAMDZFDP2\n    type: success\n    content: \"Investigation-first debugging: When tests pass but docs say they shouldn't, investigate\n      WHY before closing. In this session, discovered skill documentation was outdated rather than\n      tests being wrong - prevented false task closure and led to fixing actual issue (stale docs).\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-29T10:16:38.927Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG4M2R8569QYJMCB8GJ6XR9C\n    type: success\n    content: \"Throwaway inspection tests: Writing quick, disposable tests to inspect actual DOM/state is\n      effective debugging. DOM inspection test revealed bits-ui elements have both role='option' AND\n      data-slot attributes - concrete evidence in minutes.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-29T10:16:45.573Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG4M2YJ6TSAQ52TWWK1F2337\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Skill documentation can become stale without detection: /e2e skill claimed\n      getByRole('option') doesn't work with bits-ui when it actually does (bits-ui added proper ARIA\n      roles). No mechanism flags skill docs as potentially outdated when dependencies change. Task\n      @01KG1H91 was created based on incorrect assumption from stale docs.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-29T10:16:52.039Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG5SGK089902EVXG1FPKPX0S\n    type: success\n    content: \"Explore+Plan parallel subagent pattern for implementation tasks: Before implementing a\n      task with existing spec/notes, launch two subagents in parallel - (1) Explore agent to gather\n      codebase context (file locations, interfaces, test patterns) and (2) Plan agent to design the\n      implementation approach. Both complete before coding begins, providing thorough context AND a\n      concrete plan. Used successfully for ref normalization task - all tests passed first try.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-29T21:10:56.264Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG64RZ0E5YPAMRYH81851MJA\n    type: success\n    content: CLI --force flag pattern works well for agent/script use. inbox delete --force skips\n      confirmation. Same pattern could apply to other commands needing non-interactive mode.\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T00:27:45.039Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG6WJZFBGPPPMSNQ2H5C8Q8E\n    type: success\n    content: \"Observation triage session efficiently resolved 12 friction observations by: (1) batch\n      retrieving all observations, (2) cross-referencing AGENTS.md documentation, (3) categorizing\n      into resolvable/keep-open/historical before acting, (4) verifying obsolete items (like deleted\n      test files) before resolution\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T07:23:54.731Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG7A7ZSDZCK6RD639Q7Q02AS\n    type: friction\n    content: Test1\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T11:22:34.669Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Batch test\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T11:22:46.874Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG7A84F9WX9KXDKSQKJ6X3MX\n    type: friction\n    content: Test2\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T11:22:39.465Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Batch test\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T11:22:46.980Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG7A867AR8FGM6WE8EXM64QT\n    type: friction\n    content: Test3\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T11:22:41.259Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Batch test\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T11:22:47.048Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG7A8T9GCNWNEF22DX5P6Z15\n    type: friction\n    content: Debug1\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T11:23:01.808Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Test\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T11:23:08.702Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG7A8W996JYVJ9BGNHBRAZC3\n    type: friction\n    content: Debug2\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T11:23:03.849Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Test\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T11:23:08.817Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG7ACHTW9P6R0G5GD49WP4DY\n    type: friction\n    content: Batch1\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T11:25:04.220Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Test\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T11:25:12.344Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG7ACKM3GYQPQ6RHY81BXW72\n    type: friction\n    content: Batch2\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T11:25:06.051Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: Test\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T11:25:12.456Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG7AD09XV1EJFAN1DSW4XS4F\n    type: friction\n    content: ShellA\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T11:25:19.037Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: ShellTest\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T11:25:26.717Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG7AD2AXC4ZZBNMZW62K516P\n    type: friction\n    content: ShellB\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T11:25:21.117Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: ShellTest\n    resolved_at: 2026-01-30T11:25:26.831Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KG7ARFWPEDQZE6FH3A9RYZ1A\n    type: success\n    content: \"Test pattern: when creating multiple items in quick succession for batch operation tests,\n      use JSON mode to capture full ULIDs instead of parsing 8-char prefixes from human output. ULID\n      prefixes can collide when items are created within the same millisecond, causing test\n      deduplication to produce unexpected results. Full ULIDs are always unique.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-30T11:31:35.447Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG8PFDENWCZK15W036ZB8CX9\n    type: success\n    content: Following existing patterns (task-limit marker) made implementing new feature\n      (end-iteration) straightforward. Same file paths, detection mechanism, and cleanup lifecycle.\n    created_at: 2026-01-31T00:15:35.381Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG8RAYQJPYB4KBVHQMMGKXPV\n    type: success\n    content: \"Review feedback loop (Greptile + Claude) caught real bugs: async race condition in signal\n      handler and no-op test. Worth keeping mandatory.\"\n    created_at: 2026-01-31T00:48:06.387Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG8RB42RY7YS3283JZJ40EGS\n    type: success\n    content: User edge-case questions ('what about Ctrl+C?', 'does it work on Windows?') led to better\n      implementation. Don't rush to close - invite scrutiny.\n    created_at: 2026-01-31T00:48:11.864Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KG95K29ERJ12XFDWW44P0MPF\n    type: success\n    content: kspec search command exists and works well - found it during reflection when checking\n      coverage. Searched 'multi-ref' and got comprehensive results across specs, tasks, inbox.\n      Should use this more proactively during work.\n    created_at: 2026-01-31T04:39:43.662Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGG9KZQ5XXJ44RMQ0MW52RBF\n    type: success\n    content: \"Multi-codebase exploration via parallel subagents: Spawning 4-6 explore/research agents\n      simultaneously to analyze kspec and kynetic-bot for gap analysis, architecture comparison, and\n      Rust migration planning was highly effective. Each agent focused on one domain (CLI stack, bot\n      ecosystem, ACP, context mgmt, migration strategy) and the results synthesized into\n      comprehensive documentation.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-02T23:04:49.125Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGG9M76B5N03Z660P2B7NVH3\n    type: success\n    content: \"kspec bootstraps greenfield projects well: Initialized kynamo (Rust rewrite project) with\n      kspec to track its own development. Shadow branch, spec items for 6 implementation phases, and\n      inbox items all created smoothly. Demonstrates kspec's value beyond self-hosting - can\n      bootstrap any new project with structured planning.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-02T23:04:56.779Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGK93JZGTRSRBEB2NHW6ERBF\n    type: success\n    content: Task notes with root cause analysis and specific file list made implementation\n      straightforward - this pattern should be replicated when creating reflection-based tasks\n    created_at: 2026-02-04T02:53:35.088Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGKVNV4ZXHE1AYD8ZWA11HRF\n    type: success\n    content: Spawning a Plan agent to review completed spec/task work against the original plan catches\n      gaps (like missing traits) that the primary agent overlooked. Useful pattern for quality\n      assurance on spec creation work.\n    created_at: 2026-02-04T08:18:07.647Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGKYG2XXQ4GG2X6S87CP4HJM\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Bulk AC add missing: Adding 33 ACs required 33 individual kspec item ac add commands.\n      Would benefit from kspec item ac add-batch @ref --file acs.yaml or stdin JSON support.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-04T09:07:24.733Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: \"Batch command system exists (PRs #321/#322). Friction is documentation, not capability.\"\n    resolved_at: 2026-02-06T10:34:37.210Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KGKYGDYSYSF0WC2KEJN5P66S\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Parent relationship not persisted: item add with under flag creates items but parent field\n      is null. Also spec says parent flag but CLI requires under flag.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-04T09:07:36.025Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGKYGFQX8G25Q2ZACE340CHD\n    type: success\n    content: \"Spec split for automation eligibility: Splitting a large spec into focused child specs\n      made task-to-AC mapping clear and enabled granular automation eligibility assessment.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-04T09:07:37.854Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGM07N5F047VJTWK2R3QJZW4\n    type: friction\n    content: Test reference ambiguity with @01 prefix - When writing integration tests that create\n      plans/tasks, using generic references like @01 fails when test fixtures already contain items\n      with ULIDs starting with 01. Must use explicit slugs (--slug test-plan-1) for test isolation.\n      Affected cli-plan.test.ts and task-plan-ref.test.ts - all references needed slugs added.\n    created_at: 2026-02-04T09:37:45.647Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGM07QTQKAAQTMWERMMZHJ65\n    type: success\n    content: Schema-first implementation pattern - Defining schemas (Plan, PlansFile) first, then parser\n      functions (loadPlans, findPlanByRef), then CLI commands (plan add/get/set) created clean\n      separation. Each layer had focused tests. Pattern worked well for both plan CLI (23 tests) and\n      plan_ref field (8 tests).\n    created_at: 2026-02-04T09:37:48.375Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGM07T7QV2VV9Z6PY0TJEBHX\n    type: success\n    content: Validation ordering for better errors - When validating references, check type mismatch\n      (isTask/isSpecItem) before checking existence. Gives 'Reference X is not a plan' instead of\n      'Plan reference not found' when user passes wrong type. Applied in task add and task set\n      --plan-ref validation.\n    created_at: 2026-02-04T09:37:50.839Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGM1RX4NR7ADX19G2FTPF0S2\n    type: success\n    content: \"Pattern-following implementation: When implementing new CLI commands, examining similar\n      existing commands (e.g., derive.ts for task creation patterns, plan.ts for command structure)\n      and reusing their patterns leads to consistent, correct implementations. This approach worked\n      well for plan derive - imports, error handling, slug generation, and bidirectional updates all\n      followed established patterns, resulting in clean first implementation with no structural\n      issues.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-04T10:04:39.445Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGMX3K0D0104A8JD0NWRP526\n    type: success\n    content: \"Test-driven regex debugging proved effective: wrote comprehensive tests for plan document\n      parser's markdown section extraction (## Specs, ## Tasks, ## Implementation Notes), which\n      immediately caught regex pattern bugs (^## anchors failed to match). Fixed patterns before\n      integration, avoiding late-stage debugging. Pattern: write tests first for parsing/extraction\n      logic, especially when dealing with complex patterns or unfamiliar APIs.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-04T18:02:21.069Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGP14AGQRQ3QZFEHGY66T89J\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Test fixtures use @test-core module but many example commands in docs/tests assume @cli\n      exists. Caused global find/replace in tests when module reference didn't match. Consider: (1)\n      standardizing fixture module names to match common examples, (2) documenting fixture module\n      structure in test helpers, or (3) adding @cli as an alias/additional module in fixtures.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T04:31:53.879Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGP14D6DF0APPMFXGEZ8EJS6\n    type: success\n    content: \"Using createdSpecsMap to track specs during import solved parent reference resolution\n      elegantly. Specs created in topological order could reference earlier-created specs by slug\n      lookup in the map, working in both dry-run and real modes. Pattern: track created entities in\n      a map keyed by slug for multi-step operations with interdependencies.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T04:31:56.621Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGP14G3BD89YS91J02VH3M01\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Acceptance criteria schema requires 'id' field but this isn't obvious when writing test\n      plans or spec YAML. Parser validation fails silently - spec just doesn't appear in parsed\n      output. Better error would be: 'AC missing required field: id' at parse time. Or make id\n      optional and auto-generate if missing.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T04:31:59.595Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGP16HK67C30T8A8KMYGDFCR\n    type: friction\n    content: kspec validate output is noisy with pre-existing reference errors and alignment warnings\n      (22 ref errors, 152 alignment warnings). Makes it hard to verify whether a specific change\n      introduced new issues. A --diff or --new-only flag that shows only issues not present in the\n      previous commit would help.\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T04:33:06.662Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGP16KZRYRE4Z921QG9WE8MC\n    type: success\n    content: Plan with exact file paths, line numbers, and 'nature of change' descriptions translates\n      directly to precise edits. The plan for ralph loop fixes had a table mapping files to changes\n      — each row became one Edit tool call with no ambiguity.\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T04:33:09.112Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGP40S7D4KXBDQ38542G9ZH7\n    type: friction\n    content: Vitest replaces console.log with its own implementation that doesn't flow through\n      process.stdout.write. Tests that capture stdout.write won't see console.log output. When\n      testing code that wraps both console.log and stdout.write, spy on console.log directly\n      (vi.spyOn) and test stdout.write capture separately.\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T05:22:23.597Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGP40YN2T598YCSXZWJWWG5T\n    type: success\n    content: Tracing output flow (console.log → stdout.write chain) quickly revealed the doubled prefix\n      bug. When debugging output duplication, mapping the full write path through all\n      wrappers/interceptors identifies where multiple layers add the same content.\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T05:22:29.154Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGP3JBQP3XWSQSW83VS8YZB4\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Commander.js optional argument pattern: When a command has an optional argument like\n      .command('help [topic]'), the action handler signature must use (topic: string | undefined,\n      options) NOT (topic?: string, options?). The optional TypeScript syntax breaks Commander's\n      argument passing - options becomes an empty object. Pattern seen in task.ts commands works\n      correctly.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T05:14:31.030Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGP3JJEWMA65YMH03YMY9XKP\n    type: success\n    content: \"Test-first implementation with AC annotations: Writing tests with AC annotations (// AC:\n      @spec-ref ac-N) before implementation ensures complete coverage and creates clear\n      traceability. Pattern used in help.test.ts covered all 5 ACs systematically and caught the\n      --json flag issue early.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T05:14:37.916Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGPHG6D6WFE5AYE4V49AKBE8\n    type: success\n    content: Review agent (opus subagent) caught a real validation bug - missing required 'id' field in\n      plan document AC example. The schema check against actual parser code was the key insight.\n      Always verify examples against actual schema definitions.\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T09:18:00.102Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGPHG81NE1BNP4RX9Y7Z6YM8\n    type: friction\n    content: Committed directly to main forgetting branch protection requires PRs. Had to create branch\n      after the fact and reset. Should always create feature branch first in this repo.\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T09:18:01.781Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGQVA9RFHA4J4BEN5EAAMRJJ\n    type: success\n    content: \"Subagent delegation pattern: using Explore agent for codebase survey + general-purpose\n      agent for PR review kept main context clean and session efficient during daemon strict-mode\n      fix\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T21:28:47.119Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGQY6YCTSAKEY4FKBJTVHXEZ\n    type: success\n    content: \"Workflow run mining before prune: /reflect captured 99.4% of run content into durable\n      artifacts. Out of 181 runs with ~100 meaningful notes, only 1 contained unique info not\n      already tracked. Validates reflection-based knowledge capture approach.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T22:19:22.907Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGQY7097397E46Q8T1WZADDF\n    type: friction\n    content: \"task-work-loop has 69% abort rate (11/16 runs) — almost entirely because no eligible tasks\n      existed when started. Workflow works fine when work exists (5/5 completed all 9 steps). Root\n      cause: ralph orchestrator starts workflow without pre-checking kspec tasks ready --eligible.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T22:19:24.839Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGQY72Q4C5V3GNRWKCJGY2MZ\n    type: friction\n    content: session-reflect-loop runs too aggressively in ralph loops — 72 runs (40% of all runs),\n      chains of up to 31 consecutive executions, vast majority capture zero new items. 113 min spent\n      (19% of total workflow time) with questionable marginal value in consecutive chains. Should be\n      conditional on whether preceding task-work-loop actually completed work.\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T22:19:27.333Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGQY75ANKENZMWPXRNYWJYYP\n    type: idea\n    content: \"Workflow run telemetry: Before pruning old runs, mine them for aggregate stats (abort\n      rates, durations, sequencing patterns). Consider keeping aggregate statistics even when\n      pruning individual records to enable trend analysis. First mining found: 9.9 hrs total, PR\n      review 36%, reflect 46%, task-work-loop 6.5%.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T22:19:30.006Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGQY77CSM15MQWKTJS05N14P\n    type: friction\n    content: \"pr-review-merge consumes 36% of all workflow time (215 of 594 min). Step 1 (CI check)\n      bimodal: 30 runs under 30s but 9 over 5 min. No fast-path for trivial PRs that pass all gates\n      immediately. Consecutive chains of up to 14 suggest batch PR processing needs a dedicated\n      workflow.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T22:19:32.121Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGQYECS40M7NHKZKJPKKEK9Y\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel subagent mining pattern: spawning 3 specialized agents (notes, patterns, gaps) to\n      analyze the same dataset from different angles. Each found complementary insights the others\n      missed. Effective for pre-prune data extraction.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T22:23:27.012Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGR0NMTJDKB72NAP0YEENDF3\n    type: success\n    content: \"Subagent-driven holistic review for spec-plan design: Launching a general-purpose subagent\n      with structured review criteria (completeness, consistency, spec coverage, edge cases) caught\n      2 blockers and 7 should-fix items before plan import. Pattern: write plan doc, then have\n      subagent review against existing codebase patterns before committing.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T23:02:21.778Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGR0NPZC3QHBRCAQBQX7KV92\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Plan import drops ACs and writes malformed trait refs: Two bugs in kspec plan import\n      discovered during batch-exec plan import. (1) ACs from Specs YAML block not written to created\n      items. (2) Trait refs written without @ prefix causing schema errors. Both required manual\n      workarounds. Tasks created: @01KGR0K2, @01KGR0K5.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-05T23:02:23.980Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: \"Both bugs fixed in PR #319: createSpecItem() now preserves acceptance_criteria, and\n      trait refs are normalized with @ prefix during import.\"\n    resolved_at: 2026-02-06T00:25:02.261Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KGR5CVAAHCBBX27FD0ZN3SVQ\n    type: success\n    content: Precise plan with exact file paths, line numbers, and code diffs made the plan-import bug\n      fix session trivially fast. Plan → implement → test → PR → merge in one smooth pass with zero\n      rework.\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T00:24:56.394Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGRP6D35N9WE3EKT2KBEBC5W\n    type: success\n    content: \"Plan-import scoped notes fix: well-scoped plan with specific line numbers and code changes\n      led to zero-iteration implementation (all tests passed first try). Good pattern for future fix\n      plans.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T05:18:31.013Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGS4Y7YZCP10F4FR6V38DYW5\n    type: success\n    content: WeakMap<Command, T> annotation pattern works cleanly for adding metadata to Commander\n      commands. Avoids monkey-patching internals, is type-safe and GC-friendly, chains naturally\n      with .command() calls (markMutating(cmd.command(...))), and integrates with\n      extractCommandTree() by reading annotations during traversal. Reusable for future annotation\n      types (e.g. requires-auth, idempotent). See src/cli/command-annotations.ts for reference\n      implementation.\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T09:36:12.255Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGS89MKMBN56RX8RRGZBB50K\n    type: success\n    content: \"Subagent-reviewed AC drafts: Pattern of drafting ACs → subagent review → revise → apply\n      caught 5+ real issues (--count+--json interaction, partial success gap, missing optional flag\n      ACs, scope creep in AC-10, missing multi-trait remove symmetry). Prevented rework during\n      implementation.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T10:34:51.380Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGTF4QA30P761909YYA8KHVK\n    type: success\n    content: \"Codex CLI as external PR reviewer: running 'codex exec -m gpt-5.3-codex --sandbox\n      danger-full-access --full-auto' with a code review prompt caught a real\n      positional-arg-ordering bug that the implementing agent missed. Two independent reviewers\n      (Codex + Claude CI) found complementary issues — Codex caught the arg order bug and temp dir\n      naming, Claude CI caught the validation count mismatch and finally-block safety. Worth making\n      this a standard part of the PR review workflow.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T21:53:44.771Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: 01KGTF4Y\n    resolved_at: 2026-02-06T22:30:50.992Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KGTF4YT5Y2233BHBFZ3S8N75\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Codex sandbox can't reach api.github.com: when running codex exec with --sandbox\n      danger-full-access, network access to GitHub API was blocked, so the review comment had to be\n      posted manually. This required reading codex output, extracting the review text, and posting\n      via gh ourselves. A wrapper script or skill that handles the 'codex review then post' pattern\n      would eliminate this manual step.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T21:53:52.453Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: true\n    resolution: \"Addressed by /codex skill (PR #325). Using danger-full-access sandbox gives Codex full\n      network access including GitHub API.\"\n    resolved_at: 2026-02-06T22:30:56.697Z\n    resolved_by: \"@claude\"\n  - _ulid: 01KGTF57CRAX3CDYVTGBRS5NTV\n    type: friction\n    content: Atomic copy-back was a design gap caught by reviewers, not by tests. The plan described\n      'copy-back' as straightforward fs.cp, but both reviewers independently flagged that\n      delete-then-copy is not safe under I/O failure. Future plans involving filesystem atomicity\n      should explicitly call out failure modes in the design — the happy path isn't enough.\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T21:54:01.240Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGTF5E6S42VZ1FWESSMX2QZS\n    type: success\n    content: \"Plan-driven implementation with spec-first ACs: having 22 acceptance criteria defined\n      before coding made both implementation and testing systematic. Each test was annotated with\n      its AC reference, and the review could verify coverage by checking annotations. The\n      plan→spec→implement→test→review pipeline worked well for this medium-complexity feature.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T21:54:08.217Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGTH928DVA2CEA4FHH93M8MN\n    type: success\n    content: \"Codex self-review loop is effective: had Codex review its own skill file, it found 4\n      MUST-FIX issues (invalid CLI flags, sandbox conflicts, malformed API payloads). Then had Codex\n      review the PR with inline comments — it found 2 more issues (flag ordering, nested fences).\n      Each round of review caught real bugs that would have caused runtime failures.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T22:31:04.206Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGTH995FGYBH7S0Z0FCRJCTC\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Codex exec review subcommand has different flag parsing than codex exec: -s must go before\n      the review subcommand (codex exec -s danger-full-access review ...) not after (codex exec\n      review -s ... fails). This flag ordering quirk isn't documented in codex --help and caused a\n      runtime failure that required a fix commit.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T22:31:11.280Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGTH9GNRYXV1P230AB1KWJPH\n    type: success\n    content: \"GitHub PR review API with --input JSON file works reliably for inline comments. Pattern:\n      write structured JSON to /tmp/codex-pr-review-body.json with {event, body, comments[{path,\n      line, body}]}, then post via gh api repos/{o}/{r}/pulls/{n}/reviews --method POST --input\n      file. Codex figured out the line vs position issue on its own (first attempt used line numbers\n      which mapped to null, then corrected to diff positions).\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T22:31:18.968Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGTM42H2M0WPJGE9X7CHS7MX\n    type: success\n    content: \"Codex PR review as documentation quality gate: /codex pr caught real arg-name bugs in\n      batch JSON examples that would have caused user failures. The review→fix→push cycle was fast.\n      Worth using on all docs-heavy PRs.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T23:20:46.370Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGTNY96A6TMC4J1Y4V786JMM\n    type: success\n    content: Codex plan review as pre-import quality gate caught trait ref format bug and compound AC\n      issues. Worth making standard practice for plan imports with 3+ specs.\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T23:52:33.738Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGTNYAQNT0KVK3YTF5E7ZKYD\n    type: success\n    content: Parallel subagent research (two Explore agents) during spec-plan design phase efficiently\n      gathered session infrastructure context in ~60s instead of sequential exploration.\n    created_at: 2026-02-06T23:52:35.318Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGVCEFG5NP47A9K33GS192PD\n    type: friction\n    content: Codex PR review on self-authored PRs creates review threads that trigger\n      check-unresolved-comments CI gate. Requires manual GraphQL thread resolution + CI re-run\n      before merging. Codex skill should either skip inline comments on own PRs or auto-resolve\n      threads after posting.\n    created_at: 2026-02-07T06:25:53.158Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGVCENXDGQ8QVSC7V21SDFQT\n    type: success\n    content: Tracing ACP bugs through the chain (framing.ts → client.ts → spawner.ts → ralph.ts) was\n      efficient because the codebase has clear layering and the override mechanism (methodTimeouts)\n      was already in place. Minimal change (18 lines, 3 files) for the fix.\n    created_at: 2026-02-07T06:25:59.725Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGVDDPDMPZ9008WHBJHGHZN6\n    type: success\n    content: Task @01KGVARW had excellent root cause analysis in its notes (specific file, line numbers,\n      all call sites, exact reproduction). This made the fix trivial — under 10 minutes from start\n      to merged PR. Detailed bug reports with root cause are high-leverage.\n    created_at: 2026-02-07T06:42:56.052Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGVK9K0AR02A2MJBXWBFE5DH\n    type: success\n    content: \"Batch triage workflow: categorize inbox by theme first, quick-win deletions, then\n      one-at-a-time promotion with AskUserQuestion showing What/Why/How context. Cross-reference\n      against git log and completed tasks to catch already-done items. This pattern processed 61\n      items efficiently.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-07T08:25:32.938Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGVK9MH4RRSZT8JZP7E3089F\n    type: success\n    content: \"Implementation notes at promotion time: adding concrete implementation notes during inbox\n      promote (not after) makes tasks self-contained for future agents. Include: which files to\n      modify, patterns to follow, approximate scope.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-07T08:25:34.500Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGVK9P011GDQGTW9TJRE8FA9\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Automation triage forces context switch to spec creation: when assessing eligibility,\n      discovering a task needs a spec means switching from assessment mode to authoring mode (find\n      module, find parent, create item, add ACs, link task). Consider a guided flow or --create-spec\n      flag on task set --automation.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-07T08:25:36.001Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGWG8W1A9ZHHWCKVNVAFQM6B\n    type: success\n    content: Codex PR review caught silent bug in session log list — tasks_completed metric searched for\n      non-existent event type. Real task completions use session.update tool_call events with\n      rawInput.command containing 'task complete'. Without review, feature would ship reporting 0\n      tasks for all real sessions.\n    created_at: 2026-02-07T16:51:58.122Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGWG8YSAFS6GG225AV0AXPHW\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Session event data payloads are untyped — EventTypeSchema defines the type enum but data\n      field is z.unknown(). Had to grep through real JSONL files to discover that Ralph records task\n      completions as session.update events with sessionUpdate: 'tool_call' and rawInput.command.\n      This caused a bug that was only caught by Codex reviewing against real data.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-07T16:52:00.939Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGXHNDY3R4AC24TS1R4Q54CA\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Commander's .option() parse function (e.g. parseInt) silently pre-coerces values before\n      the action handler runs. When replacing inline validation with shared helpers, the helper\n      never sees the raw string. This caused a bug in PR #347 where derive/plan-derive still\n      accepted '3abc' as priority 3. Fix: never use Commander parse functions for options validated\n      by shared helpers.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-08T02:35:32.675Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGXHNR4TWC7Z8V6FB5NR72XF\n    type: success\n    content: Using Codex (/codex pr) as an automated second reviewer caught a real bug (Commander\n      parseInt pre-parse bypass) that manual review missed. The review-fix-re-review cycle completed\n      in one session. Worth using for every non-trivial PR.\n    created_at: 2026-02-08T02:35:43.130Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGXN2YYMYG5EEFQDM5CA6C2A\n    type: friction\n    content: Documentation tasks that update README/AGENTS.md should also check skill files\n      (.claude/skills/) for staleness on the same topics. Easy to miss because skills are a separate\n      concern. A validate --skills --docs check could catch this.\n    created_at: 2026-02-08T03:35:21.813Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGXN2Z5DF52R8XHKHYFV9XE1\n    type: success\n    content: Running 4 parallel Explore/Bash subagents to research README structure, AGENTS.md\n      structure, full CLI catalog, and recent git features simultaneously saved significant time and\n      produced comprehensive input for the docs update.\n    created_at: 2026-02-08T03:35:22.029Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGXN2ZATMXN5QJJQSMJVJZWC\n    type: friction\n    content: AGENTS.md task state transitions documented task complete as working from\n      in_progress/pending, but CLI actually requires pending_review (or --skip-review). Pre-existing\n      inaccuracy that propagated to README. Codex caught it via runtime spot-checks that I did not\n      do.\n    created_at: 2026-02-08T03:35:22.202Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGWZ26Q5N99GVBCSF23HM253\n    type: success\n    content: \"Stale index mutation pattern: when mutating items in a loop with a pre-built refIndex,\n      track created slugs in a parallel Set since refIndex won't see loop-created items. Pattern:\n      importReservedSlugs Set alongside refIndex.isSlugAvailable(). Applied in plan-import to\n      prevent cross-namespace slug collisions within a single import run.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-07T21:10:28.325Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGWZ26T7QDNKSE0F0GSX0W5T\n    type: success\n    content: \"Codex iterative review as convergence loop: codex review → fix → re-review converges on\n      correctness. 4 rounds on PR #346 found progressively deeper cross-namespace slug collision\n      gaps (duplicate_slug handling → plans missing from refIndex → stale index for import-created\n      specs → spec creation not checking importReservedSlugs). Each round caught a real bug.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-07T21:10:28.423Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGWZ26WJB8X4S3SN7GPF881Q\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Codex review depth insufficient on first pass: 4 review rounds were needed to fully\n      validate plan-import slug safety. Each fix introduced or revealed the next gap. Root cause:\n      Codex reviews surface-level patterns first (wrong API check) before deeper ones (stale index\n      across mutations). Need a way to prime Codex to reason about mutation-staleness and index\n      invalidation upfront, possibly via a review checklist or system prompt addition to the codex\n      skill.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-07T21:10:28.498Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGY73W0M9YD0PKC74CW5NSFR\n    type: success\n    content: \"Test-first doc editing: building eval scenarios before trimming AGENTS.md prevented info\n      loss. 15 scenarios + 8 stress test recall questions validated the trimmed doc (14/15 PASS, 6/8\n      PASS). Pattern: build test suite → make changes → validate → fix gaps.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-08T08:50:25.940Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGY73W3NX1Q0AV6KA9TZB2E9\n    type: success\n    content: Stress testing with real codebase exploration is more effective than synthetic padding for\n      finding doc gaps. Agent reads actual code (building 30k+ tokens of context), then answers\n      recall questions. Found 2 real degradation points (PR workflow steps, scope expansion) that\n      were reinforced.\n    created_at: 2026-02-08T08:50:26.037Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGY73W66K9NASKQBHSKY2ZHG\n    type: success\n    content: Codex as second reviewer on doc PRs caught a real inconsistency (scenario expected answer\n      vs AGENTS.md rule) and a non-existent file path. Worth running on documentation PRs, not just\n      code PRs.\n    created_at: 2026-02-08T08:50:26.118Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KGY73W872YHXWQ8VNBAQF5DD\n    type: friction\n    content: GitHub PR review thread resolution requires GraphQL mutation (resolveReviewThread). REST\n      reply endpoint posts replies but does not resolve threads. Had to discover thread node IDs via\n      GraphQL query first.\n    created_at: 2026-02-08T08:50:26.183Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHAAN8DMG4HYPXCQY05R9QT9\n    type: success\n    content: Re-baseline research findings against current code before creating specs. In CLI agent-UX\n      session, 7 of 21 recommendations from telemetry analysis were already implemented. Verifying\n      each against the codebase with parallel explore agents before speccing saved significant\n      overhead (would have created 7 unnecessary specs and 7 unnecessary tasks).\n    created_at: 2026-02-13T01:43:14.612Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHCYW7KKRGN2MV594S8YZMXH\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Commander.js parent-action option routing: when parent and subcommands define the same\n      options, Commander doesn't cleanly route them. Tried passThroughOptions (requires global\n      enablePositionalOptions, breaks --json global option), ended up using allowUnknownOption +\n      temporary Command re-parse. Pattern works but is non-idiomatic. If more command groups need\n      default actions, consider extracting this into a shared utility.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-14T02:15:03.539Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHFCMD893TQMFJWQY84RR59C\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel subagent research pattern: launching 4+ research agents simultaneously on\n      different aspects of the same question (cross-project audit, usage patterns, external\n      ecosystem, install story) produced comprehensive non-overlapping findings in ~6 minutes. Much\n      more effective than sequential investigation.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-15T00:53:56.105Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHFCMDBFRWBZ1P7NFFH8J7RA\n    type: success\n    content: \"Dual-reviewer pattern for plans: having both an internal holistic reviewer (Claude) and an\n      external reviewer (Codex) independently review the same plan catches complementary issues.\n      Internal finds code-level integration problems, external finds architectural concerns. Both\n      agreed on the same critical issues (compound ACs, inline YAML). Three revision cycles (v1\n      reviewed v2 reviewed v3) produced significantly stronger output.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-15T00:53:56.207Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHFCMDEATQ0R2Q4WW4979DQA\n    type: success\n    content: \"Iterative clarifying questions with ask tool: asking one question at a time with 3-4\n      concrete options (each with descriptions) before synthesizing research into a plan led to\n      well-informed decisions. User could respond quickly because each question had enough context\n      from the research. Better than presenting a full plan and asking for feedback.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-15T00:53:56.298Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHFPVSVMKQTR0DZCVVZ2QS6J\n    type: friction\n    content: CLI commands targeting main project files (like .claude/skills/) must use ctx.rootDir, not\n      ctx.specDir or path.dirname(ctx.specDir). The specDir is the spec content location (.kspec/ in\n      shadow mode), while rootDir is always the project root. Using dirname(specDir) fails in shadow\n      mode because .kspec/ is a worktree at the project root level. Encountered in skill render\n      command where files were written to /tmp/ instead of project root.\n    created_at: 2026-02-15T03:52:44.148Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHHR77A38WS28NJSMWG2FN0R\n    type: success\n    content: Structured interview (one question at a time with pro/con analysis) before planning leads\n      to well-reasoned architecture decisions. User engagement is higher when they see trade-offs\n      laid out clearly.\n    created_at: 2026-02-15T22:54:55.811Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHHR77CK3KME4QHCS62H0JFH\n    type: success\n    content: Running both internal Plan agent review AND Codex review-plan on the same plan catches\n      complementary issues. Internal review finds code-level gaps; Codex finds spec quality issues.\n    created_at: 2026-02-15T22:54:55.891Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHHR77EW34VT6EEW1NZHK6YF\n    type: friction\n    content: kspec batch uses kebab-case args (depends-on) but schema fields use snake_case\n      (depends_on). Inconsistency causes trial-and-error on first batch use.\n    created_at: 2026-02-15T22:54:55.964Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHKTQNHA07MZXGVJQHQAW7CA\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel subagent review of ralph loop: 5 agents reviewing different PR ranges (371-376,\n      377-384, 385-393, 394-402, test suite) completed in ~3min wall clock. Independent agents\n      finding the same duplication issues confirms real problems vs noise. Effective pattern for\n      post-loop quality review.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-16T18:17:20.683Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHKTQNN38FSK8SAEJ34G0P6F\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Ralph loop PR-by-PR review process misses cross-PR duplication accumulation. PR #381 added\n      rendering utils, #383 duplicated them in a new file, #394 consolidated render functions but\n      missed the utilities, #401 added more dead code. Each PR passes review individually but the\n      aggregate drift is significant (24 inbox items from one loop). Consider adding a\n      consolidation/cleanup iteration every N PRs or at loop end.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-16T18:17:20.803Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHQXGWG6BEEQBJ0VZ32NX2T1\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Background PR review agent can act on stale context: agent added 172-line test file for a\n      spec that was deleted during review. When running review agents in background while making\n      spec/task changes in foreground, the agent does not see those changes. Required a follow-up\n      cleanup PR.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-18T08:23:01.894Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHQXGWQJGKKY7H3KKRDXT5HQ\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Codex PR review skill always demands // AC: @spec-ref ac-N annotations, even for\n      infrastructure/cleanup tasks where ACs describe absence of code. Should skip AC annotation\n      checks when task has no spec_ref or when spec type is not user-facing behavior.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-18T08:23:02.130Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHRP78K7727DMKA224B3ZZ9Y\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Running kspec setup during development creates kspec-agents.md and .claude/skills/ in\n      project root. These are test artifacts for the kspec project itself (which uses AGENTS.md, not\n      kspec-agents.md). They trigger repeated stop hook warnings about uncommitted changes. Need\n      either: (a) test isolation so setup tests dont leak into project root, or (b) cleanup step in\n      bootstrap/dev workflow.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-18T15:34:40.999Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHRP78PDNPQAKZCPHR5XZV86\n    type: success\n    content: Multi-model PR review (Claude + Codex in parallel) caught issues that single-model review\n      missed. Codex found missing debugLog in outer catch and weak test assertions. Worth continuing\n      this pattern for non-trivial PRs.\n    created_at: 2026-02-18T15:34:41.101Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHRYZ569SCKS1HAFJK71Y2Z7\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel dual-reviewer strategy (Claude agent + Codex) is effective: Claude validates\n      correctness, Codex catches spec-alignment gaps. Use both for PRs with spec ACs.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-18T18:07:32.554Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHSG0CSF18QF1S4MMMEM3S8Y\n    type: success\n    content: Codex PR review (gpt-5.3-codex) caught a real correctness bug in drift detection\n      (hash-gating for sidecar changes) that the implementing agent missed. Codex reproduced the\n      issue locally with a concrete script. High value for code review.\n    created_at: 2026-02-18T23:05:18.896Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHSKZDW60J9YF6XTJ2WZDDE5\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Refactoring tasks without spec_ref have AC traceability gap — task-level ACs in notes\n      aren't discoverable by standard // AC: @spec-ref ac-N annotation pattern. Codex review flagged\n      this on PR #411. Options: (1) allow // AC: @task-ref ac-N, (2) require spec items even for\n      refactoring, (3) teach reviewers to check task notes. Related: @task-skill-module-split had no\n      spec_ref but defined 3 ACs in notes.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-19T00:14:41.542Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHT79F7K2QV2HKNRTD0JQTJ1\n    type: friction\n    content: Guard script bash code embedded in JS template literal makes quote escaping painful —\n      single quotes inside tr/sed cause parse errors. Consider extracting guard scripts to\n      standalone .sh files loaded at setup time instead of inline template literals.\n    created_at: 2026-02-19T05:52:13.555Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHT79FAZJZ43QN3BZA28KQYM\n    type: success\n    content: Running codex review in parallel with PR review agent caught a real security bypass\n      (split-quote git \"reset\" --hard). The dual-reviewer pattern (code-level + quality-gate)\n      provides meaningful coverage overlap.\n    created_at: 2026-02-19T05:52:13.663Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHVE714TTNEME761Y1783EYC\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Shared test fixture fragility: tests/fixtures/kynetic.meta.yaml is used by multiple test\n      files. Tests that append YAML keys (like meta.test.ts appending conventions:) collide when the\n      fixture gains new top-level keys. Caused real regression in PR #413. Consider per-test fixture\n      isolation or fixture composition helpers.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-19T17:12:28.058Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHVE7189BCM4HWW9PXWAFP37\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel agent reviews (Codex + /pr-review) found complementary issues: Codex caught test\n      annotation gaps, review agent caught shared fixture regression. Multi-reviewer pattern is\n      high-value for quality.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-19T17:12:28.169Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHVYHKAVN1G54X8C2BJYMK3X\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Invoked /spec-plan skill but wrote implementation guide instead of plan-import-format\n      document. User had explicitly said /spec-plan. Lesson: invoking a skill is not enough — must\n      follow its output format from the FIRST write. When /spec-plan is invoked for plan mode, write\n      the plan file in kspec plan import format (# Title, ## Specs with YAML code block, ## Tasks,\n      ## Implementation Notes) from the start.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-19T21:57:51.579Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHVYHKEBF6AHDDXVQZJAZV5H\n    type: success\n    content: \"Dual review pattern before plan import: running both an internal plan review agent and\n      Codex in parallel caught YAML quoting failures and substantive spec gaps (batch mode, worktree\n      detection, remote type algorithm). Reviews converged on same must-fixes, giving high\n      confidence. Always dual-review complex plan documents before importing.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-19T21:57:51.691Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHVYHKH7J728F29ZS1SGF2PM\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel consumer project exploration: launching 3 agents to explore kynetic-bot, imgen,\n      comfy-ecaj-nodes simultaneously produced convergent findings (same Quick Start pattern, same\n      hooks, same skill drift) that were far more convincing than exploring one project. Use\n      parallel exploration when researching cross-project patterns.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-19T21:57:51.783Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHW3CC8V4PDG1R22S5229TA4\n    type: success\n    content: Dual review pattern (internal Plan agent + Codex review-plan) catches complementary issues.\n      Internal agent finds architectural concerns, Codex finds format/structure issues. Convergent\n      findings give high confidence. Worth standardizing for all plan imports.\n    created_at: 2026-02-19T23:22:23.387Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHW3CCBSNYH48BKQX2Q2CNAC\n    type: success\n    content: Post-import verification agent catches data integrity issues that dry-run misses (null\n      spec_ref, missing implementation notes). Should be part of standard plan import workflow.\n    created_at: 2026-02-19T23:22:23.481Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHWVQNZV7NDDTQB5ADP4FPCW\n    type: friction\n    content: \"GitHub blocks REQUEST_CHANGES on own PR. Ralph review subagents operate under the same\n      GitHub credentials as the PR author, so they cannot post REQUEST_CHANGES reviews — only\n      COMMENT. The pr-review skill instructs posting APPROVE or REQUEST_CHANGES, but REQUEST_CHANGES\n      will always fail in self-authored PRs. Need either: (1) a separate GitHub bot account for\n      review agents, or (2) the skill should use COMMENT event with structured review content\n      instead of REQUEST_CHANGES.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-20T06:27:59.612Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHWVQP3NBA0YYME4FY9K2T0W\n    type: success\n    content: \"Dual-reviewer pattern (Claude agent + Codex) for PR review. Running both in parallel on PR\n      #424 gave convergent findings on the critical branch-lookup bug (independent discovery by\n      both). Codex also caught input validation gap that Claude missed. Different models find\n      different issues — convergent findings give high confidence, divergent findings expand\n      coverage.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-20T06:27:59.733Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHWVQP6YEJ0241DN6F4QA54J\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel review audit pattern: spawning 4 specialized subagents (worker process adherence,\n      review process adherence, code quality, spec/AC coverage) to evaluate a ralph session. Each\n      agent had a focused lens and found complementary issues. Total wall-clock time ~2 min for what\n      would have been 15+ min of sequential analysis.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-20T06:27:59.838Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHYTNNGG0B44BK1QJMRGNYZA\n    type: success\n    content: \"Dual review convergence: running both pr-review subagent and /codex review in parallel\n      catches different issues and convergent findings give high confidence. Both flagged dead\n      verifyTaskCompleted code independently.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-21T00:47:53.872Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHZ6H8YSJYW5Z9TDSA3PSRJX\n    type: success\n    content: \"Convention vs template mental model clarified: Templates carry kspec-generic content\n      (shadow branch, task lifecycle, ralph loop — same for ALL kspec projects). Conventions carry\n      project-specific rules (testing gotchas, dev setup, CI limitations — unique per project). When\n      porting content from AGENTS.md, ask: does this apply to every kspec project? Template. Only\n      this project? Convention.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-21T04:15:12.858Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHZBEEVJXMQ6TYQCP2584JKT\n    type: success\n    content: \"Spec-before-implement pattern: adding ac-6 to @agent-instruction-gen before coding the\n      noop behavior made test coverage natural and caught the right contract upfront.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-21T05:41:03.474Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KHZHZAQJE6KF7GHBEK2E79PK\n    type: friction\n    content: task get not showing descriptions meant had to grep raw YAML to verify task content after\n      batch creation. Critical gap for agents working on tasks — they cannot read the description\n      via CLI.\n    created_at: 2026-02-21T07:35:07.762Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ1A32GV14R9ZSDBQYCKFW3V\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Platform behavior assumption: PR #440 added namespace rendering\n      (.claude/skills/kspec/<id>/) without verifying Claude Code actually discovers nested skill\n      directories. It does not. Future platform integration work should verify discovery behavior\n      (e.g. create a test skill, check if Claude Code lists it) before building rendering pipelines\n      around assumed directory structures.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-21T23:55:50.683Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ1RW3898SCWYZN358637199\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Meta vs manifest confusion: skill render reads from meta (shadow branch), not template\n      manifest. Changing manifest ID without updating meta has no effect. Need to delete+re-add\n      skill via CLI.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-22T04:14:10.697Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ331N2YAJ66MXHK1W9J9HQX\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel subagent research pattern: launching 3+ research agents simultaneously to\n      investigate different aspects (code state, git history, task completions) builds comprehensive\n      evidence in ~3 minutes vs 15+ sequentially. Critical for large triage sessions (95 items).\n      Each agent gets a focused investigation scope and returns structured findings.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-22T16:31:12.990Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ3M13X05B558KQ58AXRM1K1\n    type: success\n    content: Zod superRefine pattern for status-dependent field requirements (e.g., triaged requires\n      reasoning/decided_by, acted_on requires acted_at). Should be the default approach for any\n      schema with status lifecycle — flat .optional() misses state invariants. First used in\n      triage.ts, should apply to plan.ts and similar.\n    created_at: 2026-02-22T21:28:01.184Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ3T9X36SS737DYRWW9QE9ZV\n    type: idea\n    content: |-\n      Spec gap test\n\n      Reasoning: needs spec\n    created_at: 2026-02-22T23:17:40.582Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ3X7D52RR2R6N3MS45Y7EE6\n    type: friction\n    content: \"CI timing race: when Codex posts a review comment after CI check-unresolved-comments has\n      already run, the check fails because the new thread is unresolved. Requires manual re-run\n      after resolving. Consider: (1) make check-unresolved-comments a required-last check, (2) have\n      the review workflow auto-re-run the check after resolving threads, or (3) add a gh run rerun\n      step to the codex review skill.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-23T00:08:44.450Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ4SJP2673H5V8NHJPMNNN7X\n    type: question\n    content: >-\n      [spec-gap] Include triage records in static snapshot (kspec-snapshot.json). Currently the\n      snapshot format (KspecSnapshot type) doesn't include triage records, so the triage page in\n      static/GitHub Pages mode shows an empty state with a notice instead of displaying existing\n      triage decisions read-only. AC-8 of @interactive-triage-ui expects read-only display. Needs:\n      add triage records to export snapshot, update KspecSnapshot type, add fetchTriageRecordsStatic\n      to read from snapshot.\n\n\n      Reasoning: There's a spec gap here\n    created_at: 2026-02-23T08:24:14.150Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ4SJP5TREMPX687MHBW8Y2Q\n    type: question\n    content: >-\n      [spec-gap] Cross-feature requirement pattern: How to express that core features (search,\n      validate, export) must support all entity types. When new entity type added, should\n      automatically imply tasks for core features. Options: (1) applies_to field on feature specs,\n      (2) trait on entity types like @trait-searchable, (3) validation warning for missing coverage,\n      (4) parent spec that entity types must satisfy. Surfaced when realizing search doesn't cover\n      inbox.\n\n\n      Reasoning: first item reasoning\n    created_at: 2026-02-23T08:24:14.266Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ4SNE9GHZMFEE49D3P4CKJZ\n    type: question\n    content: >-\n      [spec-gap] kspec validate @spec or @task — targeted validation that checks a single\n      spec/task's AC coverage against codebase. Not full approval, just verifies each AC has at\n      least one // AC: annotation in test files. Would make trait AC gaps immediately visible during\n      task-work. Could be used by local-review skill as a concrete check instead of relying on agent\n      diligence.\n\n\n      Reasoning: Must-have but needs spec design - targeted kspec validate for single item\n    created_at: 2026-02-23T08:25:44.496Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ4SNFHF46MCSST52ZMWXJ1R\n    type: question\n    content: >-\n      [spec-gap] Design section configuration for agents generate — allow projects to control which\n      sections appear (skills table, conventions, workflows, static templates). Key questions: where\n      does config live, include vs exclude list, defaults, custom sections, ordering, data vs\n      template distinction, migration path. See plan doc for full requirements.\n\n\n      Reasoning: Must-have but needs spec design - section configuration for agents generate\n    created_at: 2026-02-23T08:25:45.775Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ4VDK8ECG1W5T95TPP1KVF6\n    type: success\n    content: \"Pre-analyzed triage report (HTML artifact) combined with kspec batch made processing 107\n      inbox items efficient. Record-then-act pattern provided good audit trail. Pattern: analyze\n      offline, port decisions via batch.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-23T08:56:24.590Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ50B8SFBX6C1E9XRYBXZ22Q\n    type: friction\n    content: settings.json written by 3 independent subsystems during setup (installClaudeCodeHooks,\n      seedPermissions, enablePluginInProject via modifyJsonAtomic). Makes skip-when-unchanged\n      optimization impossible without either a shared coordinator or consolidating all mutations\n      into one function. Each writer reads, modifies, writes independently — interleaving prevents\n      simple content comparison.\n    created_at: 2026-02-23T10:22:31.215Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ51NBSJR7R8ZRT4RM8Q26DT\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Post-merge branch state: When inheriting a session where a PR was already merged, the\n      working directory may be on main. Always check branch (git branch --show-current) before\n      committing, and create a feature branch first. Recovering from an accidental main commit\n      requires creating a branch from HEAD and resetting main.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-23T10:45:30.546Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ5B3SSRXMPW76HE43H15EKS\n    type: success\n    content: \"Codex PR review caught a real type drift bug (Convention.validation schema mismatch)\n      during web-ui type deduplication PR. The shared-type approach works well: define in\n      @kynetic-ai/shared, re-export from web-ui, enforce with static analysis test. Dual review\n      (Codex + CI) catches complementary issues.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-23T13:30:40.824Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ63RW7JFBTJ7FWG6MQR3W71\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel subagent audit pattern: launching 4+ agents in parallel for deep-dive review of\n      ralph loop work (PR quality, functional verification, loop behavior, process adherence)\n      produced comprehensive results in ~90 seconds. Effective for post-loop quality assessment.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-23T20:41:37.266Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ63RWAKZWYCWNNG68KFBHBX\n    type: success\n    content: Dual review pattern (internal agent + Codex) for plan review catches different issue\n      categories. Internal agent found consistency gaps; Codex found concurrency risks. Convergent\n      findings give high confidence before implementation.\n    created_at: 2026-02-23T20:41:37.364Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ71CSSQNCH8KAP3YRSQT4GY\n    type: friction\n    content: \"@trait-semantic-exit-codes ACs hardcode exit code numbers (ac-2: 'exit code 1', ac-3:\n      'exit code 2', ac-4: 'exit code 3') that don't match kspec's actual EXIT_CODES scheme\n      (ERROR=1, USAGE_ERROR=2, NOT_FOUND=3, VALIDATION_FAILED=4). Every command adding trait AC test\n      coverage needs clarifying comments explaining the mapping. Fix: update trait ACs to use\n      semantic descriptions ('non-zero exit code indicating validation failure') instead of\n      hardcoded numbers, or update to match kspec's actual codes.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T05:19:18.839Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ731A1QK5ZZG40DNSERD1MD\n    type: success\n    content: \"Codex review caught fail-open bug in getBudget() — corrupt budget.json was silently\n      treated as 'no budget', effectively disabling enforcement. Changed to fail closed (only ENOENT\n      returns null, parse/validation errors propagate). Pattern: for security/enforcement code,\n      always default to the restrictive path. Codex consistently catches error-handling path issues\n      that internal review misses.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T05:47:59.416Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ73MEZ9BFMX73JFB0ZDSJVM\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Ralph task-limit-guard hook blocks gh pr create even when finishing current task work. The\n      guard treats all Bash commands equally — it can't distinguish 'creating a PR for completed\n      work' from 'starting new task work'. Result: branch pushed but PR not created, requiring next\n      iteration to finish. Consider whitelisting gh pr create or detecting PR creation context in\n      the guard.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T05:58:27.050Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ75K21W6FB80AB5567TBKAX\n    type: friction\n    content: task set --depends-on replaces all deps rather than appending. When setting multiple deps\n      in separate batch commands, only the last one survives. Must provide all deps in a single\n      call. Consider adding --add-depends-on for append semantics (similar to --relates-to on item\n      set which appends).\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T06:32:38.204Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ75RQEGNKHH82MGZK6Z4NXC\n    type: success\n    content: \"Dual plan review (internal agent + /codex review-plan) catches complementary issues:\n      internal finds design gaps and terminology problems, codex finds code-level feasibility issues\n      (missing APIs, wrong method names, breaking consumers). Convergent findings indicate high\n      confidence. Used successfully for session-start-redesign plan.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T06:35:43.952Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ77DA9VYBRRT8BCTVGAJC0T\n    type: success\n    content: \"Budget enforcement in task start integrates cleanly: check before transition, increment\n      after save, resume case handled by existing early return. The library functions\n      (checkBudget/incrementBudget) do the heavy lifting — CLI handler just wires them together.\n      Good separation of concerns between store.ts and task.ts.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T07:04:27.195Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ82GPNAENV2SH3Q8XYJBQA9\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel agent spawning for session log audit: 5 agents analyzing different log files\n      simultaneously gave comprehensive coverage. Pattern worth replicating for any multi-file\n      analysis task.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T14:58:09.706Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ8EE76AQYX301F9A34XXPWK\n    type: friction\n    content: setupTempFixtures() returns a flat dir where tempDir IS the specDir — no .kspec/ wrapper.\n      Agents that assume nested structure (path.join(tempDir, \".kspec\")) get silent test failures.\n      AGENTS.md test helpers table should note this.\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T18:26:31.242Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ8J44C5EXHEAAPHTVC71R0B\n    type: success\n    content: \"Mock ACP agent pattern (tests/fixtures/mock-acp-agent.mjs) enables fast behavioral testing\n      of ralph subprocess orchestration. Tests real env injection, budget cleanup, and signal\n      handling in ~2s each. Key enabler: --adapter-cmd flag + spawnRalphUntil helper that watches\n      output markers then kills the process.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T19:30:54.981Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ8J44G2VMVX31VYM83FP9TN\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Ralph CLI uses --max-loops but internal variables and log messages say iterations. Minor\n      naming inconsistency that causes confusion when writing tests or debugging. Example:\n      --max-loops 1 but logs Starting ralph loop (max 1 iterations).\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T19:30:55.106Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ8NDTX3WCBCC198CJAQQSZN\n    type: success\n    content: Codex PR review caught exec()+unref() not actually preventing event loop hang (stdio pipes\n      still buffered). Validated that /codex review-pr adds real value beyond rubber-stamping.\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T20:28:38.691Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ8QR2WD5BSVEMKJ4R4K0JET\n    type: success\n    content: \"Pure function pattern for hook/guard commands: exporting the core logic as a testable pure\n      function (e.g. evaluateWorktreeGuard) with stdin/process handling in the CLI layer enables\n      fast unit testing (44 tests, no I/O) while keeping the CLI integration tests minimal (7 tests\n      for protocol compliance). Replicate this pattern for future hook commands.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T21:09:11.693Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ8R05R2GJBCGFQHY966GDD8\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Plan-derived tasks with depends_on sometimes become no-ops because the dependency task\n      already implements all shared spec ACs. Seen in iteration 3:\n      @update-setup-with-migration-cleanup (all 6 ACs done by @implement-native-worktree-guard) and\n      @add-multi-harness-env-injection (all injection ACs done by\n      @implement-session-create-command). Wastes budget starts and discovery time. Potential fix:\n      plan import could warn when multiple tasks share a spec and one depends on the other, or task\n      start could auto-detect 'AC already covered' and offer to close.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T21:13:36.770Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ8X527NACE7S92M7120K6A3\n    type: friction\n    content: Session checkpoint hook fires repeatedly on research-only sessions with pre-existing\n      uncommitted changes from a different task. No way to signal this is a read-only investigation\n      session.\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T22:43:39.893Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJ8XQFTK1B2Y3CVE6XBQ2WP0\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Cross-cutting skill updates need checklist: When a concept spans multiple skills (e.g.,\n      spec context discovery in codex, pr-review, local-review, review template), updating one skill\n      without checking all related ones leads to inconsistency. Codex review on PR #511 found 4\n      findings where the dig-deeper pattern wasn't applied uniformly. Consider: a way to tag related\n      skills, or a pre-commit check that flags partial updates to skill groups.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-24T22:53:43.636Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJA6SXWS8W28JRSS5B1D227N\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel audit agents pattern: spawning 4 specialized agents (code quality, test quality,\n      non-test code, process quality) in parallel gives comprehensive coverage in ~2 min wall clock.\n      Each agent needs clear scope boundaries and structured output format.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-25T10:51:35.193Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJA9BTHR62240G32RM5P0VBP\n    type: friction\n    content: Codex skill silently exits with no output when OPENAI_API_KEY is not set. The skill\n      documents gh auth preflight but not API key validation. Agents waste time discovering this.\n      Skill should check for API key and fail fast with clear message.\n    created_at: 2026-02-25T11:36:18.744Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJAAGK1RK0N21TTF843NZWV6\n    type: success\n    content: Session test helper extraction (task @01KJ9ZDE) went smoothly. The all-fields-optional\n      SessionContext pattern works well for tests that each need a different subset of fields —\n      TypeScript structural typing handles it naturally. Reduced ~315 lines of duplication across 6\n      files into 2 shared modules. The inbox helpers needed a tempDir parameter change (closure →\n      explicit arg) which was the main mechanical transformation.\n    created_at: 2026-02-25T11:56:23.481Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJB02BPX9CYWJV8MKWKAG10R\n    type: friction\n    content: \"testUlid('PREFIX') returns identical values across calls without explicit sequence\n      argument — deterministic with default sequence=0. Caused false-positive test pass in\n      session-checkpoint-scoping tests where mySession and otherSession were identical. Fix options:\n      auto-incrementing counter, require sequence param, or rename to testUlidDeterministic to make\n      behavior obvious. testUlids() works correctly but is easy to overlook.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-25T18:13:05.885Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJBJX00DRJV7AG07Q57HQY2Y\n    type: success\n    content: \"Self-validating task pattern: created a P1 automation-eligible task whose acceptance\n      criteria IS verifying the fix works. Ralph picks it up, the task checks its own session_id\n      stamp, and the result documents whether the fix works end-to-end. Useful for testing\n      harness-level integration that can't be verified from inside an active session.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-25T23:42:13.006Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJBTMZJE38BW62X2QG6CMYYK\n    type: friction\n    content: Elysia body schema validation returns 422 (not 400) before the handler runs. When writing\n      E2E tests for daemon endpoints that have body schema validation (t.Object(...)),\n      missing/invalid body fields return 422. If the handler also has manual validation that returns\n      400, the schema check fires first. Account for this in test assertions — do not assume 400 for\n      missing body fields on Elysia-validated routes.\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T01:57:39.023Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJBW3RSM37ERH1SJ37DYHRB3\n    type: success\n    content: \"GitHub PR thread resolution requires GraphQL mutation (resolveReviewThread), not REST API.\n      REST API only supports replies. Pattern: get thread node IDs via graphql query on\n      pullRequest.reviewThreads, then loop resolveReviewThread mutations. Reliably resolved all 7\n      threads in one pass.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T02:23:12.180Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJBW3RXM0JGWW5GP8KBE53C6\n    type: friction\n    content: \"scanTestCoverage() only scanned rootDir/tests/ — missed packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/ where\n      Playwright E2E specs with AC annotations live. Fixed by extending scan to also cover the E2E\n      directory and .spec.ts/.spec.js file extensions. Risk: any future E2E test directory additions\n      would silently miss coverage until the scan list is updated. Consider making E2E scan paths\n      configurable or convention-documented.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T02:23:12.308Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJC3JSTA7DXYJ8QRZJ341KS8\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Trait N/A annotations placed inside JSDoc block comments are not machine-parseable — the\n      '* // AC:' pattern (where * is the JSDoc line prefix) does not match the scanner's '// AC:'\n      regex. Must use standalone // AC: line comments OUTSIDE any /** ... */ block. Occurred in\n      api-meta.spec.ts E2E tests, caught by Codex review, required fix commit.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T04:33:44.778Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJCVXZYRRDSMSAA2AN5TPVWR\n    type: friction\n    content: \"AC annotation verification gap: Tests annotated with wrong AC refs (e.g., Elysia 422 tests\n      annotated as ac-23 when ac-23 requires 400+{error,details}; POST body validation annotated as\n      ac-5/6/7 when those are for X-Kspec-Dir header). Fix: always run kspec item get @spec-ref and\n      read AC text before annotating tests.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T11:39:17.337Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJCXMR5S7ZZJ2DYQR7FEHXSA\n    type: success\n    content: \"Codex retrospective PR review workflow: /codex pr on merged PRs surfaces real issues.\n      Found stale dist/ bug via retro review of PR #547 that live review missed.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T12:09:11.609Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJD309GMRXFSRKWNJ6KD3MTY\n    type: friction\n    content: 'JS date validation gotcha in E2E tests: new Date(\"invalid\") returns Invalid Date but does\n      NOT throw. Tests using expect(() => new Date(x)).not.toThrow() or try/catch will always pass\n      even with malformed timestamps - false positive. Always use isNaN(new Date(x).getTime()) for\n      timestamp format validation. Caught this in api-websocket.spec.ts timestamp assertion\n      (AC-29/@trait-websocket-protocol ac-3).'\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T13:42:52.692Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJD309N30QVB8RRSD7A9J3CV\n    type: friction\n    content: \"CI check-unresolved-comments timing race in review fix cycle: When Codex posts inline\n      review comments on a PR, we push a fix commit which triggers CI immediately. The\n      check-unresolved-comments job runs BEFORE we resolve the Codex threads via GraphQL, causing it\n      to fail on the new commit. Then requires manual workflow re-run. Mitigation: always resolve\n      all review threads BEFORE pushing any fix commits during a review cycle.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T13:42:52.835Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJD309R4M9JR7EDRZPE91AEA\n    type: success\n    content: \"window.__testWs pattern for Playwright WebSocket E2E: Store native browser WebSocket in\n      window.__testWs via page.evaluate() and access it across subsequent evaluate() calls. Browser\n      context maintains the global between calls. Enables clean helper functions (connectWebSocket,\n      sendAndWaitForAck, subscribeAndWaitForBroadcast) without needing Playwright WebSocket\n      interception. Used successfully in packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-websocket.spec.ts.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T13:42:52.932Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJD6M8MHMH09W8NJ504S0D0R\n    type: friction\n    content: \"When deleting test files that cover spec ACs, kspec validate does not warn that AC\n      annotations are being removed. This means coverage regressions are only caught during Codex\n      review after the PR is up — requiring an extra fix commit. A pre-delete validate or a\n      local-review gate that checks 'these AC annotations would disappear' would catch this earlier.\n      Observed during task-delete-static-analysis-tests (PR #558): deleted web-ui-triage.test.ts\n      removed all @interactive-triage-ui ac-1..ac-8 coverage; Codex caught it, required creating\n      triage.spec.ts to recover.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T14:46:12.882Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJD933WJ6W0FBY150BET1PZN\n    type: friction\n    content: \"PR merged by review subagent while worker agent still editing files on same branch — local\n      branch switches to main automatically, all pending Edit tool changes silently lost. Caused\n      significant rework this session (re-applying all triage.spec.ts changes on new branch\n      fix/triage-ac6-session-close-error). The review subagent and worker agent operate concurrently\n      on the same branch in a fix cycle, creating a race condition. Potential mitigations: (1)\n      worker agent checks for branch changes before editing, (2) ralph serializes review subagent\n      after worker fully stops, (3) worker agent uses a local patch/stash before any branch\n      changes.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T15:29:16.691Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDFFJGEQ0R6JST5PR2JZVN4\n    type: success\n    content: Dual review pattern (internal plan review + /codex review-plan) catches complementary\n      issues — format vs substance. Worth standardizing for all plan imports.\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T17:20:56.334Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDFFJK5FZ5DBANYTJEVH6Q9\n    type: success\n    content: Shadow branch merge driver handles complex YAML conflicts (project.tasks.yaml with 38\n      divergent commits) automatically during rebase — reliable for ralph parallel sessions.\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T17:20:56.421Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDN04RM1EHW2FKD5SRD3Y95\n    type: success\n    content: Dual review pattern (plan agent + Codex) catches complementary issues. Plan agent validates\n      design, Codex validates contracts and test coverage. Worth keeping as standard practice for\n      non-trivial PRs.\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T18:57:22.197Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDQ0ZTHNQF93KHS4516B8C6\n    type: question\n    content: >-\n      [spec-gap] Merge driver: auto-resolve .kspec-agents-hash file conflicts (deterministic hash,\n      should always take latest)\n\n\n      Reasoning: Merge driver for hash file — low frequency conflict, manual resolution works\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T19:32:47.057Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDQ0ZZPZZY4TE3CX11Q65BP\n    type: question\n    content: >-\n      [spec-gap] Plan import: generate richer task descriptions from Implementation Notes section —\n      include file paths, what to change, verification steps instead of generic 'See plan...' text\n\n\n      Reasoning: Plan import richer descriptions — improvement, not blocking\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T19:32:47.222Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDQ114YVRSMJQSKZ2P4CQW0\n    type: question\n    content: >-\n      [spec-gap] Triage ac-5 says sets result_ref but delete action may not produce one. Verify\n      behavior and update spec or add test assertion.\n\n\n      Reasoning: Triage ac-5 result_ref for delete — spec may be wrong, needs verification\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T19:32:48.414Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDQ119THNSN93R18BVCPZSN\n    type: question\n    content: >-\n      [spec-gap] Triage API spec says ac-4 and ac-5 use PUT method but implementation uses POST\n      /:ref/override and POST /:ref/act. Spec needs updating to match reality.\n\n\n      Reasoning: Triage API spec PUT vs POST mismatch — spec needs updating to match implementation\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T19:32:48.570Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDQ1281SE4DYG57NR127DKN\n    type: question\n    content: >-\n      [spec-gap] @cmd-validate spec is stale — missing flags: --completeness, --staleness, --drift,\n      --alignment, --skills, --conventions (all already implemented in code). Pre-existing drift,\n      not introduced by trait AC task.\n\n\n      Reasoning: @cmd-validate spec is stale — missing 6 flags already in code. Spec drift.\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T19:32:49.537Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDQ14VW0MD9YQ077ZM45MVQ\n    type: question\n    content: >-\n      [spec-gap] kspec meta set convention: add --update-rule and --remove-rule flags. Currently the\n      only way to fix a rule is to delete the entire convention and recreate it. Surfaced during\n      skill CLI lookups task when codex review caught a wording issue in one rule.\n\n\n      Reasoning: Convention --update-rule — DX improvement, workaround is delete+recreate\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T19:32:52.221Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDR3S3ZJRMAB0M35SQEGXRM\n    type: success\n    content: \"Triage record-then-act pattern with UI review works well at scale: batch-record 41\n      decisions, user reviews/overrides in web UI, batch-act on confirmed. Clean separation of agent\n      proposals from user decisions. 12 overrides out of 41 shows useful agent-human collaboration.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T19:51:47.071Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDV6RXJE25G2B3QRF02MYW3\n    type: success\n    content: \"Codex two-pass review pattern effective: implement → codex review → fix bug found →\n      re-review clean. Caught missing previousValue in injectCodexEnv that would have broken Ralph\n      cleanup.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T20:45:50.899Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDXCB7E87A4EYJKK009VQ2K\n    type: success\n    content: Well-decomposed task descriptions with exact files and verification criteria make\n      implementation fast — the per-adapter-auto-approve task took one focused session from start to\n      merged PR.\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T21:23:50.639Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDXCBBHHBBKXDKV5Z74BX7B\n    type: success\n    content: MOCK_ACP_VERIFY_ARGS_FILE pattern extends the existing env var verification pattern cleanly\n      — behavioral test infrastructure for ACP agent spawning is now solid.\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T21:23:50.769Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDZV06SJXM9RG4YPXRXHBHQ\n    type: success\n    content: Codex PR review as iterative second reviewer catches real bugs. Two-round pattern (review →\n      fix → re-review) provides high-confidence quality gate for ralph adapter/env code.\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T22:06:48.025Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJDZV0AJP3K3RNTZ3A9ZXQFC\n    type: success\n    content: Plan-derived task descriptions with exact line numbers and numbered change steps make\n      implementation fast and focused. The plan-to-task pipeline produces high-quality work items.\n    created_at: 2026-02-26T22:06:48.146Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJEVM2Y2ZXMSY10GNP2CMBCV\n    type: friction\n    content: When posting content containing $ and angle-bracket placeholders via shell-wrapped\n      commands, interpolation can silently mutate task/PR notes; prefer literal-safe quoting or\n      file-based payloads.\n    created_at: 2026-02-27T06:12:21.570Z\n    author: Jacob Chapel\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJEVMQJJZ127WW5CHM0KQK16\n    type: success\n    content: Portable {skill:<id>} tokens with renderer-side platform resolution reduced template\n      duplication and kept Claude/Codex invocation guidance consistent across SKILL.md and\n      supporting markdown.\n    created_at: 2026-02-27T06:12:42.706Z\n    author: Jacob Chapel\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJGAE26H74N8C0ZTZ6HH5V2N\n    type: success\n    content: \"Parallel plan review (Plan agent + Codex) catches complementary issues: architectural\n      concerns vs format/structural issues. High convergence on edge cases gives confidence. Worth\n      standardizing as a dual-review step.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-27T19:50:27.281Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJGAE2A5KKANQDY4KRZWFM9W\n    type: friction\n    content: Plan-derived tasks need manual follow-up (batch set tags + note) to be automation-ready.\n      The derive step should produce standalone tasks.\n    created_at: 2026-02-27T19:50:27.397Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJGAKM10AY9KFR9JXBWFFCGX\n    type: friction\n    workflow_ref: \"@session-reflect\"\n    content: \"Core skill update UX gap: kspec skill update is version-gated, so same-version template\n      edits are skipped and require kspec skill install-core. This is non-obvious during local\n      template iteration. Improve guidance (update vs install-core) or adjust command behavior to\n      detect local template changes.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-27T19:53:29.377Z\n    author: Jacob Chapel\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n    promoted_to: \"@01KJGQVK\"\n  - _ulid: 01KJGFKJ79GAK3QF33QHRMYWJW\n    type: success\n    content: \"Holistic plan review (plan + derived specs + tasks + traits together) before any code is\n      written caught 6 spec gaps in @plan-auto-close-stale-active-sessions including missing\n      targeting semantics, liveness guard, corrupt events handling, and task dependency ordering.\n      Pattern: evaluate the full derivation tree, not just individual specs.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-27T21:20:50.410Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJGQCA1DEK15Y59X5M8N5HR5\n    type: friction\n    content: Codex PR review threads require manual GraphQL resolution + CI re-trigger before merge.\n      Multi-step dance every time codex posts inline comments.\n    created_at: 2026-02-27T23:36:41.261Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJGQCA7649GZMT2HA0Z5CXQA\n    type: success\n    content: \"Iterative codex review loop (review → fix → re-review) converges well. Three rounds on PR\n      #582 caught duplicate label, spec alignment drift, and missing test branch.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-27T23:36:41.446Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJGQKPWM32W85246H3VAWDD0\n    type: success\n    workflow_ref: \"@session-reflect\"\n    content: Targeted dry-run + focused test loop quickly exposed core-skill source-of-truth drift;\n      package-distribution test caught stale plugin artifact path immediately.\n    created_at: 2026-02-27T23:40:43.797Z\n    author: Jacob Chapel\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJGW8ZB984E1QZHMGGCHSRXR\n    type: friction\n    content: CLI tests that execute dist artifacts can produce misleading failures when dist is stale;\n      this creates avoidable debugging churn before the real code behavior is evaluated.\n    created_at: 2026-02-28T01:02:14.889Z\n    author: Jacob Chapel\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJGW8ZFQ697G7Z8T81MTXN35\n    type: success\n    content: Using a focused validate mode matrix (schema/refs/alignment/completeness/staleness +\n      combinations) quickly verified scoped semantics and prevented regressions while keeping\n      turnaround fast.\n    created_at: 2026-02-28T01:02:15.031Z\n    author: Jacob Chapel\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJJHARH9G3CT7R978K6AEBZ4\n    type: success\n    content: Isolated worktree + backup branch pattern for shadow branch recovery. Creating a backup\n      branch before destructive ops, then using /tmp worktree for experimental rebase, then patching\n      the result back as a normal commit avoided force-push entirely. This pattern should be\n      documented for future shadow branch divergence scenarios.\n    created_at: 2026-02-28T16:29:27.977Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJJHARMST4YEMPE7PYSVXSCA\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Merge driver silent data loss when --non-interactive flag missing from git config. No\n      error, no warning — just hangs on stdin and leaves files unmerged. 12 task completions lost\n      silently. Root cause: shadow.ts registration code path diverged from actual git config. Fix\n      tracked in @01KJJGJ1.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-28T16:29:28.089Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJJT519QTQXSJWRM17W06HH6\n    type: friction\n    content: Codex PR review takes 10+ minutes because npm test subagent polling is inefficient.\n      Consider instructing Codex to skip full suite and rely on CI, or use test shards instead of\n      full npm test.\n    created_at: 2026-02-28T19:03:37.528Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJJT51HXZZBH71BXK6VXKM15\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Codex PR review cannot distinguish pre-existing test failures from regressions. Flags\n      false positives (e.g. session-budget-integration flakiness on PR #590). Could pre-seed\n      known-flaky test list or compare failure counts against main baseline.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-28T19:03:37.790Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJJT51PHNAYJRJFMW7HQHMXH\n    type: success\n    content: \"Codex-then-fix cycle on PR #601 was tight: review posted, ac-9 gap caught, fixed in 1\n      commit, thread resolved, CI passed, merged. Total turnaround ~15 min including CI.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-28T19:03:37.937Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJK7F4JXEBF205YJ30MK5XS0\n    type: friction\n    content: Task budget guard blocks needs_work fix cycle transitions. kspec task start @ref fails with\n      budget exhausted even when the task is in needs_work state (an existing fix cycle, not a new\n      task start). needs_work → in_progress should be exempt from the budget guard since it is\n      resuming prior work, not starting new work. Had to skip task state transitions and create PR\n      without proper submit flow.\n    created_at: 2026-02-28T22:56:20.063Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJK7F4T0JVSCB40JEAN9PHGP\n    type: success\n    content: \"Minimal floating-promise fix pattern: storing async function result in a variable and\n      attaching .catch(() => {}) before Promise.race is the clean way to prevent Node.js 22\n      unhandled rejection crashes when a race-loser promise is later rejected by resource cleanup.\"\n    created_at: 2026-02-28T22:56:20.288Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJKCF1SNKNBV25JG0VPW9HZ6\n    type: success\n    content: \"Agent investigation breadth vs accuracy tradeoff — Explore agents are valuable for\n      surveying many files quickly but their conclusions need manual verification before acting. In\n      this session, the agent reported event listener accumulation as CRITICAL (wrong — listeners\n      registered once per spawn) while the actual bottleneck (getEventCount O(n^2)) wasn't in its\n      top findings. Pattern: use agents for breadth, verify claims against actual code, then form\n      your own root cause hypothesis.\"\n    created_at: 2026-03-01T00:23:40.085Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJN09ER284K52Q9J66N0KXT6\n    type: friction\n    content: E2E tests not in CI allowed a fundamental WebSocket upgrade bug to persist undetected.\n      Previous task closed as fixed based on unit tests passing, but E2E would have shown the server\n      never upgraded connections.\n    created_at: 2026-03-01T15:29:22.690Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJN09EX8RN1NK8K8BCVJ8Q3A\n    type: success\n    content: Progressive reproduction technique (incrementally adding middleware layers to a minimal\n      Elysia server) isolated an Elysia framework interaction bug in minutes. More effective than\n      reading framework source code.\n    created_at: 2026-03-01T15:29:22.856Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJN360FJJCGYKVE3DNNTC9HM\n    type: friction\n    content: Verifying pre-existing test failures requires stashing changes and re-running — slow\n      feedback loop. A baseline test report or CI artifact would let agents identify pre-existing\n      failures without manual stash/unstash.\n    created_at: 2026-03-01T16:19:55.507Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJN360KDR015J1E57EW2DDZX\n    type: success\n    content: \"Test-first approach for regression bugs: wrote tests that failed (confirmed bug), then\n      fixed source, then verified tests pass. Clean feedback loop — 2 failing tests before fix, 6\n      passing after. Recommend this pattern for all shadow commit gap tasks.\"\n    created_at: 2026-03-01T16:19:55.629Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJN7J5A5P8ECVFR8H7JWEX1C\n    type: friction\n    content: \"item list --json returns {items:[...]} (wrapped) while tasks list --json returns a flat\n      array. Inconsistent JSON shapes cause test type errors — kspecJson<any[]> typed as flat array\n      silently fails when the actual shape is an object wrapper. Test authors need to know to use\n      {items: Array<...>} for item list vs any[] for tasks list.\"\n    created_at: 2026-03-01T17:36:27.973Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJN7J5DSFD3YYNN0PPFP5HDD\n    type: friction\n    content: 'Item status in JSON output is a nested object {maturity: string, implementation: string}\n      not a plain string. Tests checking item.status === \"implemented\" fail silently — must use\n      item.status?.implementation. This differs from task status which IS a plain string.'\n    created_at: 2026-03-01T17:36:28.089Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJPH4ZBNDCH4J8DWYQES7M6Q\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Trait AC annotations (@trait-json-output, @trait-shadow-commit) consistently missed in new\n      test describe blocks. Two consecutive tasks (agent-definition-schema, session-model-evolution)\n      both flagged in fix cycle for missing annotations. Pattern: workers add spec-specific ACs but\n      forget inherited trait ACs. Fix: consider checklist or template reminder when adding new\n      integration test blocks.\"\n    created_at: 2026-03-02T05:43:16.085Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJPK6MMVG6FNPQQXR5MTXCGY\n    type: success\n    content: \"PR scope verification: use gh pr view N --json baseRefOid,headRefOid then git diff\n      <baseRefOid>..<headRefOid> --name-only to verify actual PR diff. This is more reliable than\n      git diff origin/main..branch when the branch base predates recent merges to main.\"\n    created_at: 2026-03-02T06:19:07.803Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJPK6MRN59TPWERX8J742KW0\n    type: friction\n    content: \"Stale PR base masquerades as scope problem: when a feature branch is based on a commit\n      that predates another merged PR, the merged PR files appear in the diff. Review says\n      out-of-scope changes. Fix is rebase onto main, not code changes. Two fix cycles consumed\n      before root cause identified. Consider adding a check in PR workflow to detect stale bases.\"\n    created_at: 2026-03-02T06:19:07.925Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJQWQ0N27F78Q4PAXYXQ98WM\n    type: friction\n    content: git -C <path> pattern prevents CWD poisoning in recovery scenarios. Agents running git\n      inside .kspec/ via cd poison the shell CWD for the rest of the session (Claude Code persists\n      CWD changes). Always use git -C /path/to/.kspec/ instead of cd .kspec/ && git. Consider adding\n      this to AGENTS.md development conventions.\n    created_at: 2026-03-02T18:24:36.002Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJR425PZWG84H2DJ0HAC6C6P\n    type: friction\n    content: 'agent.ts (PR #634) reimplemented parseInt+isNaN validation instead of using parseIntOption\n      from src/cli/validators.ts — reintroducing the partial-parse bug (parseInt(\"5abc\")===5) that\n      parseIntOption was built to fix. The helper exists and conventions doc was added after\n      @01KGWDPV, but agents implementing new CLI commands still miss it. Suggests validators.ts\n      needs more prominent callout in AGENTS.md or task templates for new CLI commands.'\n    created_at: 2026-03-02T20:33:01.663Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJR42CJ1TE15HTPGJZQ55HPE\n    type: success\n    content: \"Reading actual code before judging PR review threads saved significant work: 11 of 19 open\n      threads on PR #634 were stale (issues already fixed in the latest commit). Manual\n      thread-by-code matching took ~10 minutes but avoided implementing fixes that were already\n      done.\"\n    created_at: 2026-03-02T20:33:08.674Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJR42MWC2JSTXF3BKHVHJRT5\n    type: success\n    content: /codex pr covering both tasks in a single pass was efficient and caught a subtle bug\n      (parseInt partial-match \"5abc\"->5) that manual review missed. Dual-spec single-pass review\n      avoids duplicated context-gathering and produces tighter non-redundant findings.\n    created_at: 2026-03-02T20:33:17.196Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJR8J2KM6DRYF68M6XFYSD6P\n    type: success\n    content: Iterative Codex PR review loop (fix → push → re-review) converged in 2 passes and caught\n      layered bugs not visible in the first pass. Good pattern for PR polish cycles.\n    created_at: 2026-03-02T21:51:37.076Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJR8J2YZMHE3XHZHS56ZF5K4\n    type: friction\n    content: parseIntOption from src/cli/validators.ts repeatedly missed when implementing new CLI\n      commands — parseInt+isNaN pattern introduced 4 times in one PR. Needs more prominent discovery\n      surface (skill or convention).\n    created_at: 2026-03-02T21:51:37.439Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\n  - _ulid: 01KJRF87M7KH4FB3XH7JVAVRRV\n    type: friction\n    content: \"batch-write-buffer wiring blocked by subprocess spawn model: WriteBuffer is a\n      process-local singleton but batch-exec.ts runs each command via spawnSync as a separate\n      process. Buffer writes in the parent won't be visible to spawned child processes. Need to\n      evaluate: (a) switch to in-process command execution, or (b) use a temp file protocol where\n      children write to a staging dir and parent collects on success.\"\n    created_at: 2026-03-02T23:48:34.567Z\n    author: \"@claude\"\n    resolved: false\n    resolution: null\nskills:\n  - _ulid: 01KJ1Q8KJ7AWEXWTPV9WV350WK\n    _type: skill\n    id: help\n    name: Kspec Help\n    description: Get help with kspec commands and workflows\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.1\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJ51ST2KVBW4GRDRCH1JFM7Z\n    _type: skill\n    id: triage\n    name: Triage\n    description: Triage inbox items systematically. Records decisions with audit trail, then executes\n      actions. Supports inbox, observations, and automation eligibility triage.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.1\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJ5262GTNAS1ZN9FR4RA68BV\n    _type: skill\n    id: reflect\n    name: Session Reflection\n    description: Structured reflection at the end of work sessions. Identifies learnings, friction\n      points, and improvements for system evolution.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.1\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJ542FH6F5XDFRR8ARNC4RHW\n    _type: skill\n    id: triage-inbox\n    name: Inbox Triage\n    description: Process inbox items using the record-act pattern. Categorize, promote to spec/task,\n      merge duplicates, defer, or delete stale items with full audit trail.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.1\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJ542FJZZ4G9V3354MR2EX5N\n    _type: skill\n    id: triage-automation\n    name: Automation Triage\n    description: Assess and prepare tasks for automation eligibility. Verify spec coverage, acceptance\n      criteria, and task readiness for automated agents.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.1\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJ558NBQW0EPYRPVM3EH3E7W\n    _type: skill\n    id: writing-specs\n    name: Writing Specs\n    description: Create and maintain specification items — modules, features, requirements, acceptance\n      criteria, and traits. The source of truth for what to build.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.1\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJ55J4TWZ9PVWXMJRBKX2EDD\n    _type: skill\n    id: plan\n    name: Plan to Spec\n    description: Translate approved plans into specs and tasks. Import structured documents or create\n      incrementally. Plans persist as durable artifacts with audit trail.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.1\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJ55V684QCECG344ZT3S9XWJ\n    _type: skill\n    id: task-work\n    name: Task Work\n    description: Structured task lifecycle — start, work, note, submit, complete. Fix cycle handling,\n      scope management, loop mode for automation, and quality gates.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.1\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJ563B0CPE4C736W32ATNT8F\n    _type: skill\n    id: create-workflow\n    name: Create Workflow\n    description: Formalize repeatable patterns into trackable kspec workflows. Design steps, choose\n      triggers, create loop variants, and integrate with skills.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.1\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJ56BGT4K5WERA39VA18K1CA\n    _type: skill\n    id: review\n    name: Review\n    description: Kspec-specific review gates — spec alignment, own AC coverage, trait AC coverage, and\n      validation integration. Building block for project-specific review workflows.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.1\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJEYPTZQY0M295EE80VMTHWM\n    _type: skill\n    id: audit\n    name: audit\n    description: Comprehensive codebase audit for release readiness. Parallel exploration of docs, code,\n      config, tests, and specs to identify cruft, then interactive triage with clear action options.\n    origin: project\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags: []\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJEYPWYV7QEYPG9W9FQ3Y7NW\n    _type: skill\n    id: codex\n    name: codex\n    description: Use when the user asks to run Codex CLI (codex exec, codex resume) or wants Codex to\n      review PRs, plans, or specs. Delegates to GPT-5.3-codex with preset reasoning modes.\n    origin: project\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags: []\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJEYPYVQ2SYRQPDPMEME7WEF\n    _type: skill\n    id: e2e\n    name: e2e\n    description: E2E testing patterns for kspec web UI. Use when writing Playwright tests, debugging\n      hydration issues, or working with daemon fixtures.\n    origin: project\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags: []\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJEYQ0SWV1NJBA5P0CNFMPMA\n    _type: skill\n    id: eval-agents\n    name: eval-agents\n    description: Evaluate whether AGENTS.md provides enough context for agents to make correct\n      decisions. Spawns test agents with scenario questions and grades responses.\n    origin: project\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags: []\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJEYQ2RZMF1BM1J5KG3G4JC4\n    _type: skill\n    id: local-review\n    name: local-review\n    description: Pre-PR quality review - verify AC coverage, test quality, E2E preference, and test isolation.\n    origin: project\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags: []\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJEYQW5E3GES6RV21AR7JDQP\n    _type: skill\n    id: pr\n    name: pr\n    description: Create a pull request from current work. Handles branch creation, commits, push, and PR\n      creation. Detects branch protection and guides through the PR workflow.\n    origin: project\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags: []\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJEYQX3W594DYQAJDW12ASQX\n    _type: skill\n    id: pr-review\n    name: pr-review\n    description: Review a PR linked to a kspec task, post findings as inline comments, and merge only\n      when all quality gates pass. You NEVER fix code — you review and comment. If issues found,\n      kick back to worker.\n    origin: project\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags: []\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJEYQY32N7Q062D91P3W34ST\n    _type: skill\n    id: release\n    name: release\n    description: Create versioned releases - bump version via PR, tag, create GitHub release. CI\n      publishes to npm.\n    origin: project\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags: []\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJEYQZ29GRJM6CF18FZXBQ9E\n    _type: skill\n    id: svelte-5\n    name: svelte-5\n    description: Svelte 5 patterns, gotchas, and solutions. Use when working with Svelte 5/SvelteKit,\n      especially for reactivity, SSR, and state management issues.\n    origin: project\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags: []\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJH735R306S5WYVT3Q9KHXZF\n    _type: skill\n    id: observe\n    name: Observations\n    description: Capture and act on systemic patterns — friction, successes, questions, and ideas. The\n      feedback loop that drives process improvement.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.1\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJ51SSZ2NVZGXE32NR5TWPS9\n    _type: skill\n    id: observations\n    name: Observations\n    description: Capture and act on systemic patterns — friction, successes, questions, and ideas. The\n      feedback loop that drives process improvement.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.8.0\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\n  - _ulid: 01KJGHJ26TQ80PXZYX3FSMSSAC\n    _type: skill\n    id: observe\n    name: Observations\n    description: Capture and act on systemic patterns — friction, successes, questions, and ideas. The\n      feedback loop that drives process improvement.\n    origin: core\n    version: 0.9.0\n    platforms:\n      - claude-code\n      - codex\n    depends_on: []\n    tags:\n      - core\n    allowed_tools: []\nincludes: []\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1047,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1047,"newLines":7,"lines":["           Otherwise (new work):","             1. Submit task: kspec task submit @task","             2. Create PR: /pr skill","-            3. Stop responding — ralph handles PR review via separate subagent","+            3. Stop responding — pr-reviewer agent handles PR review via dispatch","         execution:","           mode: silent"," conventions:"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"toolName":"Edit"}},"toolCallId":"toolu_01NV3Vspn5jvmfvRTSCHxkWE","sessionUpdate":"tool_call_update","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml","oldText":"          Otherwise (new work):\n            1. Submit task: kspec task submit @task\n            2. Create PR: /pr skill\n            3. Stop responding — ralph handles PR review via separate subagent\n        execution:\n          mode: silent\nconventions:","newText":"          Otherwise (new work):\n            1. Submit task: kspec task submit @task\n            2. Create PR: /pr skill\n            3. Stop responding — pr-reviewer agent handles PR review via dispatch\n        execution:\n          mode: silent\nconventions:"}],"locations":[{"path":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/kynetic.meta.yaml","line":1047}]}}